{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018AkKgH7qHssA8CN26xa7hY","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing — contamcal-irt-calibration\n2\t\n3\t## Target Venue\n4\t- **Primary: EMNLP 2026 ARR May 25** (D006: reinstated per user directive, 12 days)\n5\t- Fallback: AAAI 2027 (Jul-Aug 2026) / ICLR 2027 (Sep 2026)\n6\t- Track: Machine Learning for NLP / Resources and Evaluation\n7\t- Aligns with EMNLP 2026 special theme \"New Missions for NLP Research\" (explicitly invites contamination/data governance work)\n8\t\n9\t## Core Insight\n10\tWhen benchmark mitigation strategies systematically fail (Emperor's New Clothes, ICML 2025: 20 strategies tested, none effective), the principled alternative is post-hoc statistical calibration — analogous to causal inference's shift from eliminating confounders to statistically controlling them. ContamCal instantiates this by augmenting IRT with contamination covariates, producing calibrated benchmark scores with Bayesian credible intervals. Theoretically grounded in educational measurement's item compromise IRT tradition (Eckerly 2017, Sinharay 2017) and explanatory IRT (De Boeck & Wilson 2004), with 3 non-trivial adaptations for LLM evaluation.\n11\t\n12\t## Core Claims (3 条)\n13\t\n14\t1. **Calibration Claim**: ContamCal's contamination-augmented 4PL IRT model (with per-benchmark γ_k) recovers true (uncontaminated) benchmark performance with statistically significant MAE improvement over baselines and nominal credible interval coverage, validated on controlled SFT contamination injection across 3+ model scales (0.5B-7B) within the Qwen2.5 family and 4 benchmarks. (Multi-family generalization is a rebuttal-ready extension via exp-014, not initial submission scope.)\n15\t\n16\t2. **Signal Effectiveness & Aggregation Claim**: Detection signal effectiveness is method-specific and scale-dependent. Systematic signal × scale × dosage AUC mapping reveals: embedding-based similarity is robust (AUC>0.95 at d005/0.5B), while Min-K++ and Self-Critique fail at small model scales (AUC≈0.5 at 0.5B). Critically, Min-K++ exhibits directional reversal at high contamination (Cohen's d = -1.2 to -2.7 at d100) — it actively misleads rather than merely failing, strengthening the case for robust aggregation. RRF fusion degrades to dominant-signal mode when constituent signals fail — honest characterization of this regime is itself a contribution. Training-free RRF remains the principled aggregation design choice (meta-circularity argument). Paper must distinguish item-level detection (within-model AUC) from model-level detection (cross-model Cohen's d). (RL regime survival deferred to exp-009 observational study; no RL-specific claims until data available.)\n17\t   **C2 contingency (Reviewer WARNING)**: \"Scale-dependent\" is currently unverified — only 0.5B data exists. If 1.5B/3B signal data shows S2/S4 remain ineffective → downgrade to \"method-specific signal effectiveness\" (drop \"scale-dependent\"), RRF discussion moves to Limitations. Min-K++ directional reversal + item-vs-model detection distinction remain novel regardless of scale outcome.\n18\t\n19\t3. **Identifiability & Uncertainty Claim**: Simulation-validated identifiability bounds (grounded in Fisher Information analysis) establish minimum signal quality thresholds. ContamCal explicitly propagates detection signal noise via measurement error modeling — Models with high-AUC signals get tighter CIs; those with degraded signals (small scale or post-RL) get appropriately wider CIs reflecting genuine epistemic uncertainty.\n20\t\n21\t## Contributions (Hierarchical — D025 rebalanced per Dream full-mode)\n22\t\n23\t### Core (co-equal; if calibration numbers weak, lean on #2 and #3)\n24\t1. ContamCal framework: two-stage pipeline (RRF provenance mapping → contamination-augmented 4PL IRT with per-benchmark γ_k) producing calibrated scores with credible intervals. ME model: report if it improves coverage; otherwise present simple model as primary and ME as ablation (D025/D8 — must clarify which model produced reported results)\n25\t2. Signal effectiveness characterization: systematic signal × scale × dosage AUC mapping revealing method-specific signal reliability. Min-K++ directional reversal (Cohen's d = -1.2 to -2.7) is the paper's most citation-worthy empirical finding per all 3 Dream tiers. Per-benchmark γ_k heterogeneity (cross-family r=0.91 if confirmed) suggests contamination susceptibility is a benchmark property\n26\t3. Fisher Information identifiability analysis: structural (AUC≥0.55) vs practical (AUC≥0.70/0.80) thresholds with measurement error attenuation — strongest theoretical contribution per all 3 Dream tiers. Elevated from Supporting (D025)\n27\t\n28\t### Supporting\n29\t4. Dual-track validation: controlled SFT injection across multiple model scales × seeds within the Qwen2.5 family (internal validity) + ecological RL case study (external validity)\n30\t5. 7 baselines + 6 quantitative evaluation metrics (incl. SBC diagnostic per D025) + bootstrap CIs for contamination-aware calibration methodology\n31\t\n32\t## Story Spine\n33\t- **Problem**: Benchmark scores are increasingly unreliable due to training data contamination. Rephrased test items inflate MMLU accuracy by 8-15 points while evading n-gram decontamination. RL post-training may further complicate detection (under investigation, exp-009). No existing method provides calibrated scores answering \"what would this model's score be if it had never seen the test data?\"\n34\t- **Existing approaches & gaps**: Detection methods (Min-K%++, ConStat, Self-Critique, KDS) flag contamination but don't calibrate scores. IRT methods (PSN-IRT, Growing Pains, ATLAS, Lalor et al. AAAI 2024) evaluate models psychometrically but don't model contamination. DCR provides adjusted accuracy but lacks uncertainty bounds and RL handling. HiBayES provides Bayesian uncertainty but ignores contamination. Emperor's New Clothes (ICML 2025) demonstrates that all 20 mitigation strategies fail — motivating post-hoc calibration. Dynamic benchmarks (LiveBench) offer an alternative but require continuous curation.\n35\t- **Our framing**: ContamCal is a \"statistical safety net\" for when mitigation is unreliable. Instead of trying to eliminate contamination from benchmarks (which doesn't work), we statistically control for it — measuring its effect and subtracting it out with proper uncertainty. Grounded in educational measurement's item compromise IRT (Eckerly 2017, Sinharay 2017) and explanatory IRT (De Boeck & Wilson 2004), with 3 non-trivial structural adaptations: (a) independent examinees → single model with joint item distribution (changes local independence semantics — see §Local Independence below), (b) binary leakage → continuous exposure scores (standard technique in explanatory IRT; our contribution is the noise propagation pipeline, not the continuous covariate itself — D025 clarification per Dream R2), (c) stable ability → regime-conditional ability (different training regimes and model scales require method-aware, scale-aware signal selection).\n36\t- **Headline result template**: \"On {benchmark}, ContamCal recovers true model performance within {X}pp MAE (bootstrap 95% CI: [{lo}, {hi}]) with {Y}% credible interval coverage, while naive scores overestimate by {Z} points under {W}% contamination dosage.\"\n37\t\n38\t## Venue Fit Risks\n39\t- **EMNLP (primary)**: Best venue fit — special theme explicitly invites contamination/data governance. Reviewers deeply familiar with NLP contamination literature (advantage: no need to motivate the problem heavily). Risk: reviewers may be less familiar with IRT/psychometric methods (mitigation: add intuitive explanations, visual pipeline overview, and connection to familiar NLP concepts like calibration/confidence estimation). Risk: may expect broader model coverage beyond Qwen2.5 (mitigation: emphasize controlled experimental design consistency, note multi-family as future work).\n40\t- **AAAI/ICLR (fallback)**: Strong fit for Bayesian/probabilistic methods. Reviewers may need more contamination context but appreciate methodological rigor.\n41\t- **Novelty positioning**: Core method is cross-disciplinary synthesis (detection signals + explanatory IRT + measurement error). NOT positioned as \"new algorithm\" — positioned as (a) signal effectiveness characterization as empirically novel finding, (b) identifiability bounds with theoretical grounding, (c) first framework bridging detection → calibration with proper UQ. RRF is a principled design choice (meta-circularity argument), not claimed as methodological contribution.\n42\t- **RL limitation**: RL models get wide CIs. This is honest — frame as \"calibration is only as good as its inputs.\" Expected regret quantification uses held-out clean benchmark as ground truth (NOT calibrated scores, to avoid circularity).\n43\t\n44\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns & Defenses\n45\t\n46\t| # | Concern | Defense | Experiment |\n47\t|---|---------|---------|------------|\n48\t| 1 | θ and γ identifiable? | Fisher Information analysis + 144-condition simulation sweep + MVP validation | exp-004 |\n49\t| 2 | Why not learned aggregation? | Meta-circularity: learned aggregator's training data may itself be contaminated; RRF is design choice, not contribution | exp-003 |\n50\t| 3 | SFT injection ≠ real contamination | Dual-track: controlled SFT (internal) + ecological RL (external) + near-zero γ check (specificity). SFT is \"best-available proxy\", acknowledged as limitation | exp-006, exp-009 |\n51\t| 4 | Scale limited to 3B | 7B controlled + 72B observational | exp-007, exp-012 |\n52\t| 5 | Why 4PL not 2PL? | MVP: 2PL γ=0.16 vs 4PL γ=0.34 at N=100; c/d necessary for realistic item modeling | exp-006 |\n53\t| 6 | Too few models (N≈15)? | D025 multi-seed strategy: 3 scales × 4+ dosages × 2-3 seeds = 24-36 models pooled. Target N≥30 minimum (N≥50 ideal). Simulation sweep (exp-004) establishes identifiability at actual N. Growing Pains pre-estimation as backup at very low N | exp-004, exp-001 |\n54\t| 7 | Noisy exposure scores | Measurement error model (exposure as noisy observation of latent τ) propagates uncertainty into posteriors automatically | exp-005 |\n55\t| 8 | No baselines | 7 baselines including DCR (EMNLP 2025) + bootstrap CIs on all comparisons | exp-006 |\n56\t| 9 | Single global γ misspecified? | Per-benchmark γ_k is primary (natural in per-benchmark fitting); joint model with shared global γ is ablation. Report both to show contamination effect heterogeneity across benchmarks | exp-006 |\n57\t| 10 | Local independence violated? | Discussed explicitly; single model responds to all items → item responses correlated through shared parameters. Empirically test via posterior predictive checks on item-level residual correlations. This is a known IRT limitation when N_examinees is small. | exp-006 |\n58\t| 11 | Single model family? | Acknowledged as limitation. Qwen2.5 chosen for controlled setup consistency (same tokenizer/architecture across scales). Multi-family validation (Llama/Pythia) prepared as rebuttal experiment (exp-014). | exp-014 (rebuttal) |\n59\t| 12 | RL regret circular? | Ground truth for regret = held-out clean benchmark scores, NOT calibrated scores. Explicitly stated | exp-009 |\n60\t| 13 | S2/S4 fail at 0.5B — RRF is just S1? | Scale-dependent: honestly report single-signal regime at 0.5B. Verify S2/S4 at 1.5B/3B. RRF value = principled aggregation when signals ARE available + graceful degradation when not. | exp-008, exp-002 |\n61\t| 14 | d100 AUC=0.5 as signal failure? | Labeling artifact: d100 contaminates ALL items → labels lose discriminative power. Must NOT be interpreted as signal degradation. Present only d005/d025 for signal evaluation. | exp-008 |\n62\t| 15 | Novelty ceiling — standard IRT synthesis? (D025, all 3 Dream tiers) | Positioned as cross-disciplinary synthesis, NOT new algorithm. Emergent value: (a) per-benchmark γ_k heterogeneity as benchmark property, (b) Min-K++ reversal as cautionary finding, (c) Fisher Info identifiability boundaries. If 4PL vs 2PL gap small → acknowledge honestly but argue c/d params needed for realistic MC modeling. Report oracle-γ ablation to decompose MAE. | exp-006 |\n63\t| 16 | Per-benchmark γ_k via separate fits, not hierarchical? (D025, [M][W]) | Per-benchmark separate fits = primary (natural, avoids cross-benchmark correlation). Hierarchical γ_k ~ Normal(μ_γ, σ_γ) as ablation to formally test heterogeneity and share info across benchmarks. Both reported. | exp-006 |\n64\t| 17 | Coverage gap — 85% vs 95% nominal? (D025, all 3 tiers) | SBC diagnostic to identify source. Possible causes: local independence violation, insufficient N, model misspecification. Report SBC alongside posterior predictive checks. If gap is from local independence → discuss as known IRT limitation with references. | exp-004, exp-006 |\n65\t| 18 | Why not just S1 alone? (D025, [M][W]) | S1-only is a baseline (#2 single-signal 2PL+γ). If RRF ≤ S1-only → present as \"S1+IRT calibration with extensible multi-signal architecture for future signals.\" Meta-circularity argument for training-free aggregation still holds. | exp-003 |\n66\t\n67\t## Evaluation Protocol (6 Metrics — D025 added SBC)\n68\t1. **Calibration error**: MAE between calibrated score and ground-truth clean accuracy, with bootstrap 95% CIs\n69\t2. **Interval coverage**: Fraction of true values within 50%/80%/95% credible intervals\n70\t3. **Interval sharpness**: Average CI width (tighter is better at fixed coverage)\n71\t4. **Ranking preservation**: Kendall's τ between calibrated and ground-truth model rankings\n72\t5. **Dose-response monotonicity**: γ effect increases monotonically with contamination dosage\n73\t6. **SBC diagnostic** (D025): Simulation-Based Calibration (Talts et al. 2018) at actual N_models and N_items to diagnose coverage gap source (model misspecification vs insufficient N vs local independence violation). CPU-only, parallelize with GPU experiments\n74\t\n75\t## Benchmarks (2 main + 2 contrasts)\n76\t1. **MMLU** — knowledge-intensive multiple-choice (14K items, subsampled 1000 for NUTS) — PRIMARY\n77\t2. **ARC-Challenge** — science reasoning multiple-choice (~1.2K items) — PRIMARY\n78\t3. **GSM8K** — mathematical reasoning free-form (~1.3K items) — NEGATIVE CONTROL (D024: open-ended tasks naturally resist contamination; signals non-discriminative; IRT correctly finds γ≈0. Paper frames as \"ContamCal identifies benchmarks not requiring calibration\")\n79\t4. **HumanEval** (appendix only) — code generation (N=164). Demoted D009: paraphrase QC 16%.\n80\t\n81\t## Baselines (7)\n82\t0. **Raw (no adjustment)** — report original benchmark scores as anchor\n83\t1. **Remove-and-rescore** — drop flagged items, rescore on remaining\n84\t2. **Single-signal 2PL+γ** — best single detection signal + simpler IRT\n85\t3. **Vanilla 4PL** — standard IRT without contamination covariate (γ=0)\n86\t4. **Linear exposure regression + bootstrap CI** — simplest post-hoc adjustment (tests if IRT complexity is necessary)\n87\t5. **Emperor's mitigation strategies** — rephrasing + option shuffling (2 representative strategies from ICML 2025)\n88\t6. **DCR fuzzy inference (EMNLP 2025)** — the only existing method producing adjusted accuracy; direct predecessor, must compare\n89\t\n90\t## Local Independence Discussion\n91\tStandard IRT assumes independent examinees. In LLM evaluation, a single model produces all item responses — responses are correlated through shared model parameters. This fundamentally alters local independence. Our approach: (1) fit IRT per-benchmark (not jointly across benchmarks) to reduce correlation scope, (2) empirically test via posterior predictive checks on item-level residual correlations, (3) discuss as known limitation with reference to fixed-effects IRT literature (Mislevy 1986). The coverage gap (if observed) may partly reflect this violation — measurement error model for exposure partially compensates by widening CIs.\n92\t\n93\t## Required Figures (Dream D2: \"zero figures\" flagged as serious deficiency)\n94\t1. Pipeline overview diagram (2-stage: RRF → 4PL+γ IRT)\n95\t2. Signal × scale × dosage AUC heatmap (exp-008) — 'regime' axis replaced by scale+dosage per D022\n96\t3. Dose-response curves (contamination dosage vs accuracy inflation, exp-001/006)\n97\t4. Identifiability phase diagram (AUC × N_models → γ recoverability, exp-004)\n98\t5. Calibrated-vs-true accuracy scatter with CIs (exp-006)\n99\t\n100\t## Citation Requirements (35+ minimum, expanded per Dream D2)\n101\tMust include: Eckerly 2017, Sinharay 2017, De Boeck & Wilson 2004, Adams et al. 1997, San Martín et al. 2009, Maris & Bechger 2009, Cormack et al. 2009 (RRF), Mislevy 1986, Lalor et al. AAAI 2024, LiveBench, TinyBenchmarks (Polo et al. 2024), KDS, CDD, contamination surveys, SBC (Talts et al. 2018), HiBayES, plus all signals/methods cited in IDEA_BRIEF.\n102\tDream D2 additions (all 3 tiers flagged):\n103\t- DIF literature: Holland & Wainer 1993, Thissen et al. 1993, Zumbo 1999 (γ_k is essentially DIF between exposure groups)\n104\t- ML calibration: Guo et al. 2017, Platt 1999 (disambiguate \"calibration\" — ours is decontamination, not probability calibration)\n105\t- Conformal prediction: Angelopoulos & Bates 2023 (alternative UQ with distribution-free coverage guarantees; discuss why Bayesian IRT preferred)\n106\t- Data attribution: Pruthi et al. 2020 (TracIn), Park et al. 2023 (TRAK) — potential additional signals, mention in Future Work\n107\t- Multidimensional IRT: Reckase 2009 (acknowledge unidimensional θ for MMLU as simplification in Limitations)\n108\tD025 additions (all 3 Dream tiers flagged):\n109\t- MIA foundations: Shokri et al. 2017 (membership inference attacks), Carlini et al. 2022 (extracting training data) — contextualize Min-K++ reversal in MIA literature\n110\t- Alternative evaluation: HELM (Liang et al. 2023), Chatbot Arena (Zheng et al. 2023) — discuss in Related Work as contamination-bypassing alternatives\n111\t- Deeper DCR engagement: Oren et al. 2024 structural comparison\n112\t- Burnell et al. 2023: multidimensional IRT for LLMs (relevant to unidimensional θ limitation)\n113\t\n114\t## Fisher Information Derivation (Dream D2: all 3 tiers flagged as critical gap)\n115\tMust derive I(γ) for 4PL+γ model in appendix. Currently stated without proof.\n116\tThe derivation must show: (1) relationship between signal AUC and γ recoverability, (2) approximation assumptions, (3) how measurement error factors in.\n117\tThis is CPU-only theoretical work — can be done in parallel with GPU experiments.\n118\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9818628c-91c5-4e2f-b68b-f03dd5fc4239","uuid":"cd2445ce-d99a-41e3-965c-ea8adc37872f","timestamp":"2026-05-14T19:32:06.200Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_13/projects/contamcal-irt-calibration/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260514T185145/best/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing — contamcal-irt-calibration\n\n## Target Venue\n- **Primary: EMNLP 2026 ARR May 25** (D006: reinstated per user directive, 12 days)\n- Fallback: AAAI 2027 (Jul-Aug 2026) / ICLR 2027 (Sep 2026)\n- Track: Machine Learning for NLP / Resources and Evaluation\n- Aligns with EMNLP 2026 special theme \"New Missions for NLP Research\" (explicitly invites contamination/data governance work)\n\n## Core Insight\nWhen benchmark mitigation strategies systematically fail (Emperor's New Clothes, ICML 2025: 20 strategies tested, none effective), the principled alternative is post-hoc statistical calibration — analogous to causal inference's shift from eliminating confounders to statistically controlling them. ContamCal instantiates this by augmenting IRT with contamination covariates, producing calibrated benchmark scores with Bayesian credible intervals. Theoretically grounded in educational measurement's item compromise IRT tradition (Eckerly 2017, Sinharay 2017) and explanatory IRT (De Boeck & Wilson 2004), with 3 non-trivial adaptations for LLM evaluation.\n\n## Core Claims (3 条)\n\n1. **Calibration Claim**: ContamCal's contamination-augmented 4PL IRT model (with per-benchmark γ_k) recovers true (uncontaminated) benchmark performance with statistically significant MAE improvement over baselines and nominal credible interval coverage, validated on controlled SFT contamination injection across 3+ model scales (0.5B-7B) within the Qwen2.5 family and 4 benchmarks. (Multi-family generalization is a rebuttal-ready extension via exp-014, not initial submission scope.)\n\n2. **Signal Effectiveness & Aggregation Claim**: Detection signal effectiveness is method-specific and scale-dependent. Systematic signal × scale × dosage AUC mapping reveals: embedding-based similarity is robust (AUC>0.95 at d005/0.5B), while Min-K++ and Self-Critique fail at small model scales (AUC≈0.5 at 0.5B). Critically, Min-K++ exhibits directional reversal at high contamination (Cohen's d = -1.2 to -2.7 at d100) — it actively misleads rather than merely failing, strengthening the case for robust aggregation. RRF fusion degrades to dominant-signal mode when constituent signals fail — honest characterization of this regime is itself a contribution. Training-free RRF remains the principled aggregation design choice (meta-circularity argument). Paper must distinguish item-level detection (within-model AUC) from model-level detection (cross-model Cohen's d). (RL regime survival deferred to exp-009 observational study; no RL-specific claims until data available.)\n   **C2 contingency (Reviewer WARNING)**: \"Scale-dependent\" is currently unverified — only 0.5B data exists. If 1.5B/3B signal data shows S2/S4 remain ineffective → downgrade to \"method-specific signal effectiveness\" (drop \"scale-dependent\"), RRF discussion moves to Limitations. Min-K++ directional reversal + item-vs-model detection distinction remain novel regardless of scale outcome.\n\n3. **Identifiability & Uncertainty Claim**: Simulation-validated identifiability bounds (grounded in Fisher Information analysis) establish minimum signal quality thresholds. ContamCal explicitly propagates detection signal noise via measurement error modeling — Models with high-AUC signals get tighter CIs; those with degraded signals (small scale or post-RL) get appropriately wider CIs reflecting genuine epistemic uncertainty.\n\n## Contributions (Hierarchical — D025 rebalanced per Dream full-mode)\n\n### Core (co-equal; if calibration numbers weak, lean on #2 and #3)\n1. ContamCal framework: two-stage pipeline (RRF provenance mapping → contamination-augmented 4PL IRT with per-benchmark γ_k) producing calibrated scores with credible intervals. ME model: report if it improves coverage; otherwise present simple model as primary and ME as ablation (D025/D8 — must clarify which model produced reported results)\n2. Signal effectiveness characterization: systematic signal × scale × dosage AUC mapping revealing method-specific signal reliability. Min-K++ directional reversal (Cohen's d = -1.2 to -2.7) is the paper's most citation-worthy empirical finding per all 3 Dream tiers. Per-benchmark γ_k heterogeneity (cross-family r=0.91 if confirmed) suggests contamination susceptibility is a benchmark property\n3. Fisher Information identifiability analysis: structural (AUC≥0.55) vs practical (AUC≥0.70/0.80) thresholds with measurement error attenuation — strongest theoretical contribution per all 3 Dream tiers. Elevated from Supporting (D025)\n\n### Supporting\n4. Dual-track validation: controlled SFT injection across multiple model scales × seeds within the Qwen2.5 family (internal validity) + ecological RL case study (external validity)\n5. 7 baselines + 6 quantitative evaluation metrics (incl. SBC diagnostic per D025) + bootstrap CIs for contamination-aware calibration methodology\n\n## Story Spine\n- **Problem**: Benchmark scores are increasingly unreliable due to training data contamination. Rephrased test items inflate MMLU accuracy by 8-15 points while evading n-gram decontamination. RL post-training may further complicate detection (under investigation, exp-009). No existing method provides calibrated scores answering \"what would this model's score be if it had never seen the test data?\"\n- **Existing approaches & gaps**: Detection methods (Min-K%++, ConStat, Self-Critique, KDS) flag contamination but don't calibrate scores. IRT methods (PSN-IRT, Growing Pains, ATLAS, Lalor et al. AAAI 2024) evaluate models psychometrically but don't model contamination. DCR provides adjusted accuracy but lacks uncertainty bounds and RL handling. HiBayES provides Bayesian uncertainty but ignores contamination. Emperor's New Clothes (ICML 2025) demonstrates that all 20 mitigation strategies fail — motivating post-hoc calibration. Dynamic benchmarks (LiveBench) offer an alternative but require continuous curation.\n- **Our framing**: ContamCal is a \"statistical safety net\" for when mitigation is unreliable. Instead of trying to eliminate contamination from benchmarks (which doesn't work), we statistically control for it — measuring its effect and subtracting it out with proper uncertainty. Grounded in educational measurement's item compromise IRT (Eckerly 2017, Sinharay 2017) and explanatory IRT (De Boeck & Wilson 2004), with 3 non-trivial structural adaptations: (a) independent examinees → single model with joint item distribution (changes local independence semantics — see §Local Independence below), (b) binary leakage → continuous exposure scores (standard technique in explanatory IRT; our contribution is the noise propagation pipeline, not the continuous covariate itself — D025 clarification per Dream R2), (c) stable ability → regime-conditional ability (different training regimes and model scales require method-aware, scale-aware signal selection).\n- **Headline result template**: \"On {benchmark}, ContamCal recovers true model performance within {X}pp MAE (bootstrap 95% CI: [{lo}, {hi}]) with {Y}% credible interval coverage, while naive scores overestimate by {Z} points under {W}% contamination dosage.\"\n\n## Venue Fit Risks\n- **EMNLP (primary)**: Best venue fit — special theme explicitly invites contamination/data governance. Reviewers deeply familiar with NLP contamination literature (advantage: no need to motivate the problem heavily). Risk: reviewers may be less familiar with IRT/psychometric methods (mitigation: add intuitive explanations, visual pipeline overview, and connection to familiar NLP concepts like calibration/confidence estimation). Risk: may expect broader model coverage beyond Qwen2.5 (mitigation: emphasize controlled experimental design consistency, note multi-family as future work).\n- **AAAI/ICLR (fallback)**: Strong fit for Bayesian/probabilistic methods. Reviewers may need more contamination context but appreciate methodological rigor.\n- **Novelty positioning**: Core method is cross-disciplinary synthesis (detection signals + explanatory IRT + measurement error). NOT positioned as \"new algorithm\" — positioned as (a) signal effectiveness characterization as empirically novel finding, (b) identifiability bounds with theoretical grounding, (c) first framework bridging detection → calibration with proper UQ. RRF is a principled design choice (meta-circularity argument), not claimed as methodological contribution.\n- **RL limitation**: RL models get wide CIs. This is honest — frame as \"calibration is only as good as its inputs.\" Expected regret quantification uses held-out clean benchmark as ground truth (NOT calibrated scores, to avoid circularity).\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns & Defenses\n\n| # | Concern | Defense | Experiment |\n|---|---------|---------|------------|\n| 1 | θ and γ identifiable? | Fisher Information analysis + 144-condition simulation sweep + MVP validation | exp-004 |\n| 2 | Why not learned aggregation? | Meta-circularity: learned aggregator's training data may itself be contaminated; RRF is design choice, not contribution | exp-003 |\n| 3 | SFT injection ≠ real contamination | Dual-track: controlled SFT (internal) + ecological RL (external) + near-zero γ check (specificity). SFT is \"best-available proxy\", acknowledged as limitation | exp-006, exp-009 |\n| 4 | Scale limited to 3B | 7B controlled + 72B observational | exp-007, exp-012 |\n| 5 | Why 4PL not 2PL? | MVP: 2PL γ=0.16 vs 4PL γ=0.34 at N=100; c/d necessary for realistic item modeling | exp-006 |\n| 6 | Too few models (N≈15)? | D025 multi-seed strategy: 3 scales × 4+ dosages × 2-3 seeds = 24-36 models pooled. Target N≥30 minimum (N≥50 ideal). Simulation sweep (exp-004) establishes identifiability at actual N. Growing Pains pre-estimation as backup at very low N | exp-004, exp-001 |\n| 7 | Noisy exposure scores | Measurement error model (exposure as noisy observation of latent τ) propagates uncertainty into posteriors automatically | exp-005 |\n| 8 | No baselines | 7 baselines including DCR (EMNLP 2025) + bootstrap CIs on all comparisons | exp-006 |\n| 9 | Single global γ misspecified? | Per-benchmark γ_k is primary (natural in per-benchmark fitting); joint model with shared global γ is ablation. Report both to show contamination effect heterogeneity across benchmarks | exp-006 |\n| 10 | Local independence violated? | Discussed explicitly; single model responds to all items → item responses correlated through shared parameters. Empirically test via posterior predictive checks on item-level residual correlations. This is a known IRT limitation when N_examinees is small. | exp-006 |\n| 11 | Single model family? | Acknowledged as limitation. Qwen2.5 chosen for controlled setup consistency (same tokenizer/architecture across scales). Multi-family validation (Llama/Pythia) prepared as rebuttal experiment (exp-014). | exp-014 (rebuttal) |\n| 12 | RL regret circular? | Ground truth for regret = held-out clean benchmark scores, NOT calibrated scores. Explicitly stated | exp-009 |\n| 13 | S2/S4 fail at 0.5B — RRF is just S1? | Scale-dependent: honestly report single-signal regime at 0.5B. Verify S2/S4 at 1.5B/3B. RRF value = principled aggregation when signals ARE available + graceful degradation when not. | exp-008, exp-002 |\n| 14 | d100 AUC=0.5 as signal failure? | Labeling artifact: d100 contaminates ALL items → labels lose discriminative power. Must NOT be interpreted as signal degradation. Present only d005/d025 for signal evaluation. | exp-008 |\n| 15 | Novelty ceiling — standard IRT synthesis? (D025, all 3 Dream tiers) | Positioned as cross-disciplinary synthesis, NOT new algorithm. Emergent value: (a) per-benchmark γ_k heterogeneity as benchmark property, (b) Min-K++ reversal as cautionary finding, (c) Fisher Info identifiability boundaries. If 4PL vs 2PL gap small → acknowledge honestly but argue c/d params needed for realistic MC modeling. Report oracle-γ ablation to decompose MAE. | exp-006 |\n| 16 | Per-benchmark γ_k via separate fits, not hierarchical? (D025, [M][W]) | Per-benchmark separate fits = primary (natural, avoids cross-benchmark correlation). Hierarchical γ_k ~ Normal(μ_γ, σ_γ) as ablation to formally test heterogeneity and share info across benchmarks. Both reported. | exp-006 |\n| 17 | Coverage gap — 85% vs 95% nominal? (D025, all 3 tiers) | SBC diagnostic to identify source. Possible causes: local independence violation, insufficient N, model misspecification. Report SBC alongside posterior predictive checks. If gap is from local independence → discuss as known IRT limitation with references. | exp-004, exp-006 |\n| 18 | Why not just S1 alone? (D025, [M][W]) | S1-only is a baseline (#2 single-signal 2PL+γ). If RRF ≤ S1-only → present as \"S1+IRT calibration with extensible multi-signal architecture for future signals.\" Meta-circularity argument for training-free aggregation still holds. | exp-003 |\n\n## Evaluation Protocol (6 Metrics — D025 added SBC)\n1. **Calibration error**: MAE between calibrated score and ground-truth clean accuracy, with bootstrap 95% CIs\n2. **Interval coverage**: Fraction of true values within 50%/80%/95% credible intervals\n3. **Interval sharpness**: Average CI width (tighter is better at fixed coverage)\n4. **Ranking preservation**: Kendall's τ between calibrated and ground-truth model rankings\n5. **Dose-response monotonicity**: γ effect increases monotonically with contamination dosage\n6. **SBC diagnostic** (D025): Simulation-Based Calibration (Talts et al. 2018) at actual N_models and N_items to diagnose coverage gap source (model misspecification vs insufficient N vs local independence violation). CPU-only, parallelize with GPU experiments\n\n## Benchmarks (2 main + 2 contrasts)\n1. **MMLU** — knowledge-intensive multiple-choice (14K items, subsampled 1000 for NUTS) — PRIMARY\n2. **ARC-Challenge** — science reasoning multiple-choice (~1.2K items) — PRIMARY\n3. **GSM8K** — mathematical reasoning free-form (~1.3K items) — NEGATIVE CONTROL (D024: open-ended tasks naturally resist contamination; signals non-discriminative; IRT correctly finds γ≈0. Paper frames as \"ContamCal identifies benchmarks not requiring calibration\")\n4. **HumanEval** (appendix only) — code generation (N=164). Demoted D009: paraphrase QC 16%.\n\n## Baselines (7)\n0. **Raw (no adjustment)** — report original benchmark scores as anchor\n1. **Remove-and-rescore** — drop flagged items, rescore on remaining\n2. **Single-signal 2PL+γ** — best single detection signal + simpler IRT\n3. **Vanilla 4PL** — standard IRT without contamination covariate (γ=0)\n4. **Linear exposure regression + bootstrap CI** — simplest post-hoc adjustment (tests if IRT complexity is necessary)\n5. **Emperor's mitigation strategies** — rephrasing + option shuffling (2 representative strategies from ICML 2025)\n6. **DCR fuzzy inference (EMNLP 2025)** — the only existing method producing adjusted accuracy; direct predecessor, must compare\n\n## Local Independence Discussion\nStandard IRT assumes independent examinees. In LLM evaluation, a single model produces all item responses — responses are correlated through shared model parameters. This fundamentally alters local independence. Our approach: (1) fit IRT per-benchmark (not jointly across benchmarks) to reduce correlation scope, (2) empirically test via posterior predictive checks on item-level residual correlations, (3) discuss as known limitation with reference to fixed-effects IRT literature (Mislevy 1986). The coverage gap (if observed) may partly reflect this violation — measurement error model for exposure partially compensates by widening CIs.\n\n## Required Figures (Dream D2: \"zero figures\" flagged as serious deficiency)\n1. Pipeline overview diagram (2-stage: RRF → 4PL+γ IRT)\n2. Signal × scale × dosage AUC heatmap (exp-008) — 'regime' axis replaced by scale+dosage per D022\n3. Dose-response curves (contamination dosage vs accuracy inflation, exp-001/006)\n4. Identifiability phase diagram (AUC × N_models → γ recoverability, exp-004)\n5. Calibrated-vs-true accuracy scatter with CIs (exp-006)\n\n## Citation Requirements (35+ minimum, expanded per Dream D2)\nMust include: Eckerly 2017, Sinharay 2017, De Boeck & Wilson 2004, Adams et al. 1997, San Martín et al. 2009, Maris & Bechger 2009, Cormack et al. 2009 (RRF), Mislevy 1986, Lalor et al. AAAI 2024, LiveBench, TinyBenchmarks (Polo et al. 2024), KDS, CDD, contamination surveys, SBC (Talts et al. 2018), HiBayES, plus all signals/methods cited in IDEA_BRIEF.\nDream D2 additions (all 3 tiers flagged):\n- DIF literature: Holland & Wainer 1993, Thissen et al. 1993, Zumbo 1999 (γ_k is essentially DIF between exposure groups)\n- ML calibration: Guo et al. 2017, Platt 1999 (disambiguate \"calibration\" — ours is decontamination, not probability calibration)\n- Conformal prediction: Angelopoulos & Bates 2023 (alternative UQ with distribution-free coverage guarantees; discuss why Bayesian IRT preferred)\n- Data attribution: Pruthi et al. 2020 (TracIn), Park et al. 2023 (TRAK) — potential additional signals, mention in Future Work\n- Multidimensional IRT: Reckase 2009 (acknowledge unidimensional θ for MMLU as simplification in Limitations)\nD025 additions (all 3 Dream tiers flagged):\n- MIA foundations: Shokri et al. 2017 (membership inference attacks), Carlini et al. 2022 (extracting training data) — contextualize Min-K++ reversal in MIA literature\n- Alternative evaluation: HELM (Liang et al. 2023), Chatbot Arena (Zheng et al. 2023) — discuss in Related Work as contamination-bypassing alternatives\n- Deeper DCR engagement: Oren et al. 2024 structural comparison\n- Burnell et al. 2023: multidimensional IRT for LLMs (relevant to unidimensional θ limitation)\n\n## Fisher Information Derivation (Dream D2: all 3 tiers flagged as critical gap)\nMust derive I(γ) for 4PL+γ model in appendix. Currently stated without proof.\nThe derivation must show: (1) relationship between signal AUC and γ recoverability, (2) approximation assumptions, (3) how measurement error factors in.\nThis is CPU-only theoretical work — can be done in parallel with GPU experiments.\n","numLines":118,"startLine":1,"totalLines":118}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017qCsdcLMVPceJCn5NUqeG4","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"stage1_signal_pipeline\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"在exp-001产出的全部contaminated+clean模型(0.5B/1.5B/3B × d000/d005/d025/d100 × 2 seeds)上 计算4个detection signals: S1(embedding semantic retrieval), S2(Min-K%++), S3(ConStat performance gap), S4(Self-Critique entropy collapse)。 0.5B数据已完成(exp_002_signals_05B)，此处展开1.5B和3B的预测。\\n\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"S1_auc_05B_d005_mmlu\": 0.953,\n7\t      \"S1_auc_05B_d005_gsm8k\": 0.988,\n8\t      \"S1_auc_05B_d005_arc\": 0.995,\n9\t      \"S2_auc_05B_d005_mean\": 0.465,\n10\t      \"S4_auc_05B_d005_mean\": 0.481,\n11\t      \"S1_auc_15B_d005_mmlu\": 0.965,\n12\t      \"S1_auc_15B_d005_gsm8k\": 0.991,\n13\t      \"S1_auc_15B_d005_arc\": 0.996,\n14\t      \"S2_auc_15B_d005_mmlu\": 0.72,\n15\t      \"S2_auc_15B_d005_gsm8k\": 0.68,\n16\t      \"S2_auc_15B_d005_arc\": 0.74,\n17\t      \"S3_auc_15B_d005_mmlu\": 0.67,\n18\t      \"S3_auc_15B_d005_arc\": 0.71,\n19\t      \"S4_auc_15B_d005_mmlu\": 0.7,\n20\t      \"S4_auc_15B_d005_gsm8k\": 0.66,\n21\t      \"S4_auc_15B_d005_arc\": 0.73,\n22\t      \"S1_auc_3B_d005_mmlu\": 0.972,\n23\t      \"S1_auc_3B_d005_gsm8k\": 0.993,\n24\t      \"S1_auc_3B_d005_arc\": 0.997,\n25\t      \"S2_auc_3B_d005_mmlu\": 0.8,\n26\t      \"S2_auc_3B_d005_gsm8k\": 0.76,\n27\t      \"S2_auc_3B_d005_arc\": 0.83,\n28\t      \"S3_auc_3B_d005_mmlu\": 0.74,\n29\t      \"S3_auc_3B_d005_arc\": 0.78,\n30\t      \"S4_auc_3B_d005_mmlu\": 0.77,\n31\t      \"S4_auc_3B_d005_gsm8k\": 0.73,\n32\t      \"S4_auc_3B_d005_arc\": 0.8,\n33\t      \"S2_d100_cohens_d_15B_mmlu\": -1.52,\n34\t      \"S2_d100_cohens_d_15B_arc\": -1.38,\n35\t      \"S2_d100_cohens_d_3B_mmlu\": -2.31,\n36\t      \"S2_d100_cohens_d_3B_arc\": -2.67,\n37\t      \"signal_computation_time_per_model_hours\": 1.5,\n38\t      \"total_gpu_hours\": 18\n39\t    },\n40\t    \"tables\": [\n41\t      {\n42\t        \"name\": \"Table: Signal AUC × Scale × Dosage Heatmap (d005 within-model)\",\n43\t        \"description\": \"4 signals × 3 scales × 3 benchmarks矩阵。Cells标注AUC值和95% bootstrap CI。 Color coding: green(≥0.70), yellow(0.55-0.70), red(<0.55)。 展示S2/S4从0.5B red到3B green的scale-dependent transition。\\n\"\n44\t      },\n45\t      {\n46\t        \"name\": \"Table: Cross-model Cohen's d at d100 (d100 vs d000)\",\n47\t        \"description\": \"3 signals × 3 scales × 3 benchmarks。标注Cohen's d值和方向箭头。 突出Min-K++ reversal: 0.5B d=-1.98, 3B d=-2.67。\\n\"\n48\t      }\n49\t    ],\n50\t    \"figures\": [],\n51\t    \"analysis\": \"S2/S4在≥1.5B恢复effectiveness验证了'scale-dependent signal reliability'叙事。 这不仅是empirical observation——它反映了小模型(0.5B)缺乏足够capacity来形成 可检测的memorization痕迹或self-evaluation能力。ARC在所有signals表现最好(items最少、 contamination signal-to-noise ratio最高)。GSM8K的S2/S4 AUC略低于MMLU/ARC， 与open-ended format降低memorization检测力一致。S1保持scale-invariant高AUC(≥0.95) 确认embedding retrieval作为robust anchor signal。Min-K++ reversal随scale增强 (Cohen's d从-1.52到-2.67)是论文最强citation-worthy发现——它证明了naively relying on individual signals can ACTIVELY mislead(不仅仅是fail)。\\n\\n\\nS2(Min-K++)和S4(Self-Critique)的scale-dependent recovery机制： (a) Min-K++依赖token-level perplexity异常检测memorization。0.5B模型容量不足， 即使见过contaminated paraphrases也难以形成持久的token-level记忆痕迹(AUC≈0.47)。 1.5B容量足以保留item-specific记忆，contaminated items呈现显著更低的token surprise(AUC→0.72)。 3B容量充裕，memorization痕迹更清晰(AUC→0.80)。 (b) Self-Critique依赖模型自我评估能力(entropy collapse on seen items)。0.5B的 self-evaluation不可靠(AUC≈0.48)。1.5B emergence of metacognitive capability使得 模型对seen items表现出过度自信(更低entropy)，AUC→0.70。3B self-evaluation更稳定(AUC→0.77)。 (c) S1(embedding retrieval)基于外部sentence-transformer匹配，不依赖目标模型能力， 因此AUC在所有scale一致≥0.95。 (d) Min-K++ d100 reversal持续且scale-dependent：d100将ALL items标记为contaminated， 模型整体token-level distribution向training data shift，导致clean items的perplexity 反而更接近contaminated distribution→Min-K++反向判断。3B模型更充分地拟合d100 training data， reversal更强(Cohen's d=-2.67)。 (e) S3(ConStat)在1.5B/3B恢复，因为larger models对original vs paraphrased items的 performance gap更稳定、更可检测。0.5B的noise floor太高。\\n\"\n52\t  },\n53\t  {\n54\t    \"name\": \"rrf_aggregation_ablation\",\n55\t    \"description\": \"RRF融合4个signals为composite per-item exposure score。 消融实验: (a) RRF vs equal-weight rank averaging, (b) single-signal only (×4), (c) calibration-based weighted RRF, (d) FP injection robustness, (e) degraded 2-signal mode (ConStat+Self-Critique for closed-weight).\\n\",\n56\t    \"results\": {\n57\t      \"rrf_composite_auc_05B_d005_mmlu\": 0.955,\n58\t      \"rrf_composite_auc_05B_d005_arc\": 0.995,\n59\t      \"rrf_vs_best_single_delta_05B\": 0.002,\n60\t      \"rrf_composite_auc_15B_d005_mmlu\": 0.975,\n61\t      \"rrf_composite_auc_15B_d005_arc\": 0.998,\n62\t      \"rrf_vs_best_single_delta_15B\": 0.015,\n63\t      \"rrf_composite_auc_3B_d005_mmlu\": 0.985,\n64\t      \"rrf_composite_auc_3B_d005_arc\": 0.999,\n65\t      \"rrf_vs_best_single_delta_3B\": 0.02,\n66\t      \"rrf_vs_equal_weight_delta_auc_3B\": 0.008,\n67\t      \"weighted_rrf_vs_rrf_delta_3B\": 0.003,\n68\t      \"fp_injection_10pct_auc_retention\": 0.96,\n69\t      \"fp_injection_20pct_auc_retention\": 0.91,\n70\t      \"degraded_2signal_auc_3B_mmlu\": 0.79,\n71\t      \"degraded_2signal_auc_3B_arc\": 0.82,\n72\t      \"s1_only_auc_3B_mmlu\": 0.972,\n73\t      \"s2_only_auc_3B_mmlu\": 0.8,\n74\t      \"s3_only_auc_3B_mmlu\": 0.74,\n75\t      \"s4_only_auc_3B_mmlu\": 0.77\n76\t    },\n77\t    \"tables\": [\n78\t      {\n79\t        \"name\": \"Table: RRF Ablation Comparison (3B d005)\",\n80\t        \"description\": \"Rows: RRF-4sig, RRF-3sig(no S3), S1-only, S2-only, S3-only, S4-only, equal-weight, weighted-RRF, 2-signal(S3+S4)。 Columns: MMLU AUC, ARC AUC, GSM8K AUC, Mean AUC, Δ vs S1-only。\\n\"\n81\t      },\n82\t      {\n83\t        \"name\": \"Table: FP Robustness (RRF AUC at varying FP injection rates)\",\n84\t        \"description\": \"Rows: FP rate 0%, 5%, 10%, 15%, 20%。 Columns: MMLU, ARC, GSM8K composite AUC。\\n\"\n85\t      }\n86\t    ],\n87\t    \"figures\": [],\n88\t    \"analysis\": \"RRF的真正价值在≥1.5B multi-signal regime中显现——当constituent signals各自捕获 不同contamination facets时，rank fusion产生genuine information gain。在0.5B single-signal regime，RRF优雅退化且不引入harm(不比S1-only差)。 Meta-circularity argument得到empirical支持：calibration-based weighting仅+0.3pp， 远不值得引入对training data quality的dependency。Training-free RRF保持设计选择定位。 2-signal mode在3B AUC≥0.79确认closed-weight applicability。\\n\\n\\n(a) 0.5B regime: S2/S3/S4均≈random(AUC<0.55)，RRF退化为S1-only模式。 RRF composite AUC ≈ S1 AUC(+0.002)，因为random signals的RRF ranks 不系统性偏移有效S1的排序。这是graceful degradation——RRF不会因无效信号 而比最佳单信号更差(rank fusion的鲁棒性)。 (b) 1.5B regime: S2/S4恢复(AUC 0.68-0.74)，RRF聚合3-4个above-chance signals。 Rank fusion的互补性在此显现：S1基于training-data proximity，S2基于memorization trace， S4基于metacognition——不同failure modes提供正交information。AUC提升1.5pp over S1-only。 (c) 3B regime: 4个signals全部AUC>0.74，RRF提升2.0pp over S1-only。这是RRF展示 genuine aggregation value的最佳展示区间。 (d) RRF vs equal-weight: RRF对高排名items给予更大权重(reciprocal rank)， 优于uniform averaging 0.8pp——因为top-ranked items的agreement更informative。 (e) Calibration-based weighted RRF仅+0.3pp over vanilla RRF——marginal improvement 不值得引入calibration dependency(meta-circularity argument仍成立)。 (f) FP injection: RRF容忍10% FP rate(AUC保持96%)，20%时下降至91%。 Rank fusion对sparse FP鲁棒因为FP不会系统性地在多个signals中出现。 (g) 2-signal degraded mode(S3+S4, no logits/embeddings): AUC 0.79-0.82 at 3B， sufficient for closed-weight calibration但CI会更宽。\\n\"\n89\t  },\n90\t  {\n91\t    \"name\": \"irt_calibration_and_baselines\",\n92\t    \"description\": \"在exp-001/003产出的controlled models上拟合4PL+γ IRT(Stan NUTS)。 PRIMARY: per-benchmark fitting with per-benchmark γ_k。 ABLATION: joint fitting with global γ, hierarchical γ_k ~ Normal(μ_γ, σ_γ)。 N_models ≥ 30 (3 scales × 4 dosages × 2-3 seeds)。 Compare against 7 baselines。Report 6 evaluation metrics。\\n\",\n93\t    \"results\": {\n94\t      \"max_rhat\": 1.007,\n95\t      \"min_ess_gamma\": 520,\n96\t      \"min_ess_theta\": 380,\n97\t      \"divergent_transitions\": 0,\n98\t      \"fit_time_mmlu_1000items_min\": 35,\n99\t      \"fit_time_arc_1172items_min\": 28,\n100\t      \"fit_time_gsm8k_1319items_min\": 32,\n101\t      \"n_models_pooled\": 32,\n102\t      \"gamma_k_mmlu_mean\": 0.28,\n103\t      \"gamma_k_mmlu_sd\": 0.06,\n104\t      \"gamma_k_arc_mean\": 0.38,\n105\t      \"gamma_k_arc_sd\": 0.07,\n106\t      \"gamma_k_gsm8k_mean\": 0.06,\n107\t      \"gamma_k_gsm8k_sd\": 0.04,\n108\t      \"gamma_k_humaneval_mean\": 0.12,\n109\t      \"gamma_k_humaneval_sd\": 0.08,\n110\t      \"gamma_k_cv_across_benchmarks\": 0.52,\n111\t      \"gamma_ci_excludes_zero_mmlu\": true,\n112\t      \"gamma_ci_excludes_zero_arc\": true,\n113\t      \"gamma_ci_excludes_zero_gsm8k\": false,\n114\t      \"gamma_ci_excludes_zero_humaneval\": true,\n115\t      \"gamma_ci_excludes_zero_rate\": 0.88,\n116\t      \"mae_contam_cal_pp_mean\": 2.1,\n117\t      \"mae_contam_cal_pp_std\": 0.4,\n118\t      \"ci_coverage_95pct\": 92,\n119\t      \"ci_coverage_80pct\": 82,\n120\t      \"ci_coverage_50pct\": 53,\n121\t      \"ci_sharpness_avg_width_pp\": 5.8,\n122\t      \"kendall_tau\": 0.91,\n123\t      \"dose_response_monotonicity_violations\": 0,\n124\t      \"sbc_rank_uniformity_pvalue\": 0.23,\n125\t      \"mae_mmlu_pp\": 1.8,\n126\t      \"mae_arc_pp\": 2.3,\n127\t      \"mae_gsm8k_pp\": 1.1,\n128\t      \"mae_humaneval_pp\": 3.8,\n129\t      \"mae_raw_no_adjustment_pp\": 9.2,\n130\t      \"mae_remove_rescore_pp\": 6.8,\n131\t      \"mae_single_signal_2pl_gamma_pp\": 3.9,\n132\t      \"mae_vanilla_4pl_no_gamma_pp\": 7.4,\n133\t      \"mae_linear_regression_pp\": 4.3,\n134\t      \"mae_emperor_mitigation_pp\": 8.1,\n135\t      \"mae_dcr_pp\": 4.6,\n136\t      \"mae_improvement_vs_dcr_pp\": 2.5,\n137\t      \"mae_improvement_vs_best_baseline_pp\": 1.8,\n138\t      \"mae_global_gamma_pp\": 3.1,\n139\t      \"mae_hierarchical_gamma_pp\": 2.3,\n140\t      \"hierarchical_mu_gamma\": 0.22,\n141\t      \"hierarchical_sigma_gamma\": 0.14,\n142\t      \"mae_oracle_gamma_pp\": 1.4,\n143\t      \"oracle_vs_estimated_gap_pp\": 0.7,\n144\t      \"ci_coverage_95_me_model\": 93,\n145\t      \"ci_coverage_95_simple_model\": 88,\n146\t      \"ci_sharpness_me_vs_simple_ratio\": 1.12\n147\t    },\n148\t    \"tables\": [\n149\t      {\n150\t        \"name\": \"Table: Main Results — Calibration Metrics × 8 Methods\",\n151\t        \"description\": \"Rows: Raw, Remove-rescore, Single-signal 2PL+γ, Vanilla 4PL, Linear regression, Emperor mitigation, DCR, ContamCal(ours)。 Columns: MAE(pp)±bootstrap CI, 95% Coverage, 80% Coverage, CI Width(pp), Kendall τ, Monotonicity violations。Bolded: ContamCal wins on all metrics。 Bottom row: Δ vs DCR with significance marker。\\n\"\n152\t      },\n153\t      {\n154\t        \"name\": \"Table: Per-benchmark γ_k Estimates\",\n155\t        \"description\": \"Rows: MMLU, ARC-Challenge, GSM8K, HumanEval。 Columns: γ_k posterior mean, 95% CI, CI excludes 0?, effect size interpretation。 Highlight: CV(γ_k)=0.52，支撑'contamination susceptibility is benchmark property'。\\n\"\n156\t      },\n157\t      {\n158\t        \"name\": \"Table: Calibration Metrics Decomposed by Benchmark\",\n159\t        \"description\": \"Rows: 4 benchmarks。Columns: MAE, Coverage, Sharpness, per-benchmark notes。 GSM8K row highlighted as negative control (γ≈0, MAE lowest)。\\n\"\n160\t      },\n161\t      {\n162\t        \"name\": \"Table: Model Ablation — Global γ vs Per-benchmark γ_k vs Hierarchical\",\n163\t        \"description\": \"3 rows × same metric columns。Per-benchmark γ_k primary; global γ loses 1.0pp MAE; hierarchical γ_k intermediate (formal heterogeneity test)。\\n\"\n164\t      }\n165\t    ],\n166\t    \"figures\": [],\n167\t    \"analysis\": \"exp-006是论文核心实验。MAE=2.1pp(±0.4)显著优于DCR的4.6pp(Δ=2.5pp, p<0.01 bootstrap test)。 Coverage 92%接近但未达95% nominal——SBC p=0.23确认这不是model misspecification， 而是local independence violation的已知IRT limitation(single model→correlated item responses)。 ME model部分弥补(88%→93%)但complete correction需要更复杂的correlated-error model (超出本文scope，acknowledged in Limitations)。Per-benchmark γ_k的CV=0.52是 论文的structural insight——contamination susceptibility取决于benchmark format和content characteristics， 不是model property。Oracle γ分析(gap=0.7pp)量化了detection signal quality的calibration ceiling—— future work的better signals可directly translate to tighter calibration。\\n\\n\\n(a) NUTS收敛(R̂<1.01, ESS>400): exp-004 simulation sweep已在N=50/AUC=0.80验证 MCMC quality(0 divergence, max R̂=1.010, min ESS=439)。Real data N=32(multi-seed pooling) 在simulation验证范围内。MMLU subsampled至1000 items降低计算负担同时保留statistical power。 (b) Per-benchmark γ_k heterogeneity(CV=0.52): ARC γ_k=0.38最大——science reasoning MC items 格式固定且答案模式可记忆，contamination直接提升正确选项probability。MMLU γ_k=0.28中等—— 14K items diversity dilutes per-item memorization benefit。GSM8K γ_k≈0.06—— open-ended generation format天然抵抗contamination(即使见过问题，仍需自主推理得出答案)， 正确扮演negative control角色。HumanEval γ_k=0.12小——code generation部分受益于pattern recall 但functional correctness仍需正确逻辑。 (c) γ CI排除0的rate=0.88(≈7/8 benchmark-conditions排除0)：MMLU/ARC/HumanEval排除0， GSM8K不排除(γ≈0.06±0.04, CI包含0)。这恰好验证了negative control和contamination susceptibility is benchmark property的论点。 (d) MAE=2.1pp: IRT通过item-level response patterns检测contamination效应——即使 average benchmark accuracy change仅1-2pp(1.5B/3B MMLU)，contaminated items呈现 concentrated 15-20pp per-item accuracy boost(被95% uncontaminated items稀释)。 IRT的γ_k × e_ij项精确捕获这种item-level effect。Counterfactual(e=0)移除此effect 后recovery误差主要来自：(i)θ-γ posterior correlation残余(~0.5pp)， (ii)item subsample noise for MMLU(~0.3pp)，(iii)per-item exposure score noise(~0.5pp)。 (e) CI coverage 92% vs nominal 95%: 3pp gap的主要来源是local independence violation (single model responds to all items→item responses correlated through shared parameters)。 ME model通过propagating exposure noise部分补偿(88%→93%)。SBC诊断p=0.23确认 model specification本身正确(coverage gap来自local independence, not model misspecification)。 (f) Kendall τ=0.91: 校准后model ranking高度保留。少量ranking变化来自high-dosage models的calibration adjustment。 (g) Dose-response monotonicity: γ effect单调递增(d005<d025<d100)，0 violations。 0.5B的negative overall accuracy与positive γ共存不违反单调性——γ衡量的是per-item contamination benefit(正)，而θ降低反映overall SFT degradation(负)。 (h) DCR MAE=4.6pp vs ContamCal 2.1pp: DCR缺乏per-item resolution和Bayesian UQ， 只能做benchmark-level fuzzy adjustment。Linear regression MAE=4.3pp因为linear assumption 不能捕获IRT的nonlinear item-response relationship。 (i) Oracle γ gap=0.7pp: exposure score noise贡献了~0.7pp MAE overhead， 说明signal quality是calibration precision的binding constraint。\\n\"\n168\t  },\n169\t  {\n170\t    \"name\": \"scale_bridging_7b\",\n171\t    \"description\": \"Qwen2.5-7B controlled SFT injection at 4 dosage levels(d000/d005/d025/d100)。 验证calibration accuracy和signal effectiveness scaling至7B。 LoRA SFT on 1×H100, ~6h per run。\\n\",\n172\t    \"results\": {\n173\t      \"sft_time_per_run_hours\": 6.5,\n174\t      \"total_gpu_hours\": 26,\n175\t      \"sft_d000_final_loss\": 0.92,\n176\t      \"sft_d100_final_loss\": 0.98,\n177\t      \"eval_d000_mmlu\": 0.735,\n178\t      \"eval_d000_gsm8k\": 0.798,\n179\t      \"eval_d000_arc\": 0.874,\n180\t      \"eval_d000_humaneval\": 0.268,\n181\t      \"eval_d005_mmlu\": 0.742,\n182\t      \"eval_d005_gsm8k\": 0.801,\n183\t      \"eval_d005_arc\": 0.882,\n184\t      \"eval_d025_mmlu\": 0.756,\n185\t      \"eval_d025_arc\": 0.893,\n186\t      \"eval_d100_mmlu\": 0.779,\n187\t      \"eval_d100_gsm8k\": 0.806,\n188\t      \"eval_d100_arc\": 0.908,\n189\t      \"eval_d100_humaneval\": 0.28,\n190\t      \"mmlu_inflation_pp\": 4.4,\n191\t      \"arc_inflation_pp\": 3.4,\n192\t      \"gsm8k_inflation_pp\": 0.8,\n193\t      \"S1_auc_7B_d005_mean\": 0.978,\n194\t      \"S2_auc_7B_d005_mean\": 0.85,\n195\t      \"S4_auc_7B_d005_mean\": 0.82,\n196\t      \"S2_d100_cohens_d_7B\": -2.85,\n197\t      \"mae_with_7B_pp\": 2.0,\n198\t      \"ci_coverage_95_with_7B\": 93,\n199\t      \"gamma_k_mmlu_with_7B\": 0.31,\n200\t      \"gamma_k_arc_with_7B\": 0.4\n201\t    },\n202\t    \"tables\": [\n203\t      {\n204\t        \"name\": \"Table: 7B Dose-Response Accuracy\",\n205\t        \"description\": \"Rows: d000, d005, d025, d100。Columns: MMLU, ARC, GSM8K, HumanEval。 Compare inflation pattern with 0.5B/1.5B/3B。\\n\"\n206\t      }\n207\t    ],\n208\t    \"figures\": [],\n209\t    \"analysis\": \"7B数据是scale-bridging的关键——它证明了contamination inflation随model capacity增长， 在practical model sizes(7B)处达到可测量且需要校准的水平(MMLU +4.4pp)。 同时S2/S4 AUC进一步提升验证了scale-dependent signal narrative的completeness。 7B加入IRT pool后calibration quality marginal improvement表明N=32已接近saturation。\\n\\n\\n(a) 7B contamination inflation更大(MMLU +4.4pp, ARC +3.4pp vs 1.5B/3B的<2pp)： 7B capacity足以在LoRA SFT中同时维持general capability和memorize contaminated items。 0.5B/1.5B/3B的smaller capacity forced a tradeoff(0.5B: memorization hurts general, 1.5B/3B: memorization barely helps)。7B跨过了capacity threshold使memorization productively translate to benchmark inflation。这验证了contamination是real-world concern at practical model scales。 (b) GSM8K inflation仅0.8pp：7B对GSM8K的CoT reasoning在SFT后保持稳定(vs 3B catastrophic forgetting)，但open-ended format仍然抵抗contamination inflation。 (c) S2/S4 AUC在7B进一步提升(S2: 0.85, S4: 0.82)：更大模型的memorization痕迹更深， token-level signals更清晰。Min-K++ reversal也更强(Cohen's d=-2.85)——7B更充分拟合 d100 training data distribution。 (d) Adding 7B to IRT pool(N_models→38-40)改善calibration(MAE 2.1→2.0pp, coverage 92→93%)： 更多examinees + wider ability range改善θ estimation和γ identifiability。 γ_k_mmlu增加(0.28→0.31)因为7B贡献了更清晰的contamination signal。\\n\"\n210\t  },\n211\t  {\n212\t    \"name\": \"signal_survival_analysis\",\n213\t    \"description\": \"系统评估detection signal reliability across scales和dosages。 0.5B数据已完成(exp_008_signal_survival_v4)。 扩展到1.5B/3B + Instruct/RL proxy models。 输出: signal × scale × dosage AUC heatmap(论文Figure 2)。\\n\",\n214\t    \"results\": {\n215\t      \"S1_d005_auc_05B_mean\": 0.979,\n216\t      \"S2_d005_auc_05B_mean\": 0.465,\n217\t      \"S4_d005_auc_05B_mean\": 0.481,\n218\t      \"S1_d100_cross_cohens_d_05B\": 3.6,\n219\t      \"S2_d100_cross_cohens_d_05B\": -1.98,\n220\t      \"S4_d100_cross_cohens_d_05B\": 0.45,\n221\t      \"effective_signals_at_05B\": 1,\n222\t      \"S1_d005_auc_15B_mean\": 0.97,\n223\t      \"S2_d005_auc_15B_mean\": 0.72,\n224\t      \"S4_d005_auc_15B_mean\": 0.7,\n225\t      \"S1_d100_cross_cohens_d_15B\": 3.85,\n226\t      \"S2_d100_cross_cohens_d_15B\": -1.52,\n227\t      \"S4_d100_cross_cohens_d_15B\": 0.88,\n228\t      \"effective_signals_at_15B\": 3,\n229\t      \"S1_d005_auc_3B_mean\": 0.98,\n230\t      \"S2_d005_auc_3B_mean\": 0.8,\n231\t      \"S4_d005_auc_3B_mean\": 0.77,\n232\t      \"S1_d100_cross_cohens_d_3B\": 4.2,\n233\t      \"S2_d100_cross_cohens_d_3B\": -2.31,\n234\t      \"S4_d100_cross_cohens_d_3B\": 1.15,\n235\t      \"effective_signals_at_3B\": 3,\n236\t      \"S4_instruct_vs_base_sensitivity\": 0.68,\n237\t      \"S2_instruct_degradation_pct\": 15,\n238\t      \"S1_instruct_stable\": true,\n239\t      \"s2_auc_070_threshold_scale\": \"~1.2B (interpolated)\",\n240\t      \"s4_auc_070_threshold_scale\": \"~1.4B (interpolated)\"\n241\t    },\n242\t    \"tables\": [\n243\t      {\n244\t        \"name\": \"Table: Full Signal × Scale × Dosage AUC Matrix\",\n245\t        \"description\": \"Grand matrix: 3 signals(S1/S2/S4) × 3 scales(0.5B/1.5B/3B) × 3 dosages(d005/d025/d100) × 3 benchmarks(MMLU/ARC/GSM8K)。d005 cells = within-model AUC; d100 cells = cross-model Cohen's d。Color: green/yellow/red threshold coding。\\n\"\n246\t      },\n247\t      {\n248\t        \"name\": \"Table: Instruct/RL Proxy Signal Comparison\",\n249\t        \"description\": \"Rows: Base, Instruct, RL-proxy。Columns: S1/S2/S4 sensitivity metrics。\\n\"\n250\t      }\n251\t    ],\n252\t    \"figures\": [],\n253\t    \"analysis\": \"exp-008是Core Contribution #2的实证基础。3个key findings： (1) Scale-dependent emergence: S2/S4从0.5B random(AUC≈0.47)到3B effective(AUC≈0.80/0.77)， transition at ~1.2-1.4B。这不是arbitrary——对应LLM capability emergence in memorization and metacognition。 (2) Min-K++ reversal(d=-1.98 at 0.5B, d=-2.31 at 3B): 最强citation-worthy发现。 Warning: naive use of Min-K++ at high contamination ACTIVELY MISLEADS。机制analysis (全量memorization→perplexity distribution shift→reversal)提供explanatory depth。 (3) Item-level vs cross-model detection范式区分：d005用within-model AUC(item discrimination)， d100用cross-model Cohen's d(model discrimination)。d100 AUC=0.5是labeling artifact (all items contaminated→no discriminative labels)，不是signal failure。\\n\\n\\n(a) Signal survival pattern由model capacity驱动：0.5B缺乏token-level memorization depth(S2 fails)和metacognitive self-evaluation(S4 fails)。1.5B是transition point—— S2/S4 emergent capabilities使AUC跨过0.70 practical threshold。3B consolidates。 S1(embedding retrieval)依赖external encoder，始终stable。 (b) Min-K++ reversal机制：d100将所有items加入training data，模型的token-level distribution 整体shift。Min-K++基于\\\"low perplexity tokens\\\"检测memorization，但当EVERYTHING is memorized， baseline perplexity distribution itself shifts→clean items的relative perplexity paradoxically更接近contaminated profile→reversal。3B模型更充分学习d100 distribution→ reversal更强(d=-2.31 vs 0.5B d=-1.98)。 (c) S4(Self-Critique)d100 cross-model Cohen's d从0.5B=0.45增至3B=1.15： larger models的self-evaluation对contaminated items更consistently confident， cross-model effect size增长。 (d) Instruct/RL proxy: Instruct models经过RLHF/DPO，token-level distributions 进一步shift。S2(Min-K++)在Instruct models上AUC降低~15%(perplexity patterns被RLHF扰动)， 但S4(Self-Critique)在Instruct models上因为enhanced instruction-following能力 实际上更有效(sensitivity=0.68)。S1保持stable因为embedding retrieval不依赖target model。 (e) Scale transition thresholds通过linear interpolation估计：S2在~1.2B达到AUC=0.70， S4在~1.4B。这与LLM capability emergence literature一致。\\n\"\n254\t  },\n255\t  {\n256\t    \"name\": \"rl_observational_case_study\",\n257\t    \"description\": \"对existing RL-trained models (Qwen2.5-Instruct 0.5B/1.5B/3B/7B, DeepSeek-R1-Distill-1.5B/7B) 应用ContamCal pipeline。 Observational study——directional external validity, not full quantitative validation。 Near-zero γ check on known-clean benchmark作为specificity test。\\n\",\n258\t    \"results\": {\n259\t      \"S1_auc_instruct_3B\": 0.94,\n260\t      \"S2_auc_instruct_3B\": 0.62,\n261\t      \"S4_auc_instruct_3B\": 0.71,\n262\t      \"S1_auc_deepseek_r1_7B\": 0.91,\n263\t      \"gamma_mmlu_instruct_models\": 0.18,\n264\t      \"gamma_mmlu_instruct_ci_width\": 0.22,\n265\t      \"gamma_arc_instruct_models\": 0.25,\n266\t      \"gamma_arc_instruct_ci_width\": 0.19,\n267\t      \"gamma_mmlu_deepseek_r1\": 0.14,\n268\t      \"gamma_mmlu_deepseek_ci_width\": 0.28,\n269\t      \"gamma_clean_benchmark_mean\": 0.02,\n270\t      \"gamma_clean_benchmark_ci_includes_zero\": true,\n271\t      \"specificity_pass\": true,\n272\t      \"top5_selection_changes_uncal_vs_cal\": 2,\n273\t      \"top5_selection_changes_cal_vs_remove_rescore\": 1,\n274\t      \"regret_reduction_pct\": 35,\n275\t      \"ci_width_rl_vs_sft_ratio\": 1.8\n276\t    },\n277\t    \"tables\": [\n278\t      {\n279\t        \"name\": \"Table: RL Model Calibration Results\",\n280\t        \"description\": \"Rows: 6 RL models。Columns: Raw score, Calibrated score, 95% CI, γ estimate, Signal AUC(S1/S2/S4), CI width ratio vs SFT。\\n\"\n281\t      },\n282\t      {\n283\t        \"name\": \"Table: Expected Regret Analysis\",\n284\t        \"description\": \"Top-5 rankings under: Raw, Remove-rescore, ContamCal。 Highlight position changes and regret scores。\\n\"\n285\t      }\n286\t    ],\n287\t    \"figures\": [],\n288\t    \"analysis\": \"Observational case study提供directional external validity。Key insights: (1) RL post-training partially但未完全消除SFT-phase contamination(γ>0 for RL models)。 (2) ContamCal honestly widens CIs when signal quality degrades(CI width ratio 1.8×)—— 这是feature not bug，正确反映epistemic uncertainty。 (3) Specificity test通过确认framework不会over-calibrate clean benchmarks。 (4) 2 top-5 ranking changes demonstrate practical impact for model selection decisions。 Framed as \\\"directional\\\"——no ground truth for RL models, acknowledged in Limitations。\\n\\n\\n(a) Signal quality on RL models degraded但non-trivially：RLHF/DPO改变token-level distributions使S2(Min-K++)AUC降至0.62(from SFT baseline ~0.80 at 3B)——RL optimization partially erases memorization traces。S4(Self-Critique)更robust(AUC=0.71)因为 RLHF actually enhances self-evaluation capability。S1(embedding)保持高AUC(0.94) 因为independent of target model。 (b) γ estimates with wide CIs(width 0.19-0.28 vs SFT的~0.06-0.08)： RL models的exposure scores更noisy(S2 degraded)→ME model propagates这些noise into wider posteriors。这是honest uncertainty——calibration精度受限于input signal quality， 系统正确报告了这种limitation。 (c) Instruct models γ_mmlu=0.18(moderate)：RL post-training未fully消除SFT-phase contamination。Qwen2.5-Instruct很可能在SFT phase包含了benchmark-adjacent data。 γ比controlled SFT experiments低(0.28)因为RL optimization partially corrects memorized shortcuts。 (d) DeepSeek-R1-Distill γ=0.14 with wider CI：reasoning-distilled model的contamination profile不同于standard RLHF。更宽CI反映更不确定的exposure estimation。 (e) Specificity pass(γ_clean≈0.02, CI includes 0)：关键validation——ContamCal不会 对genuinely clean benchmarks产生false positive校准adjustment。 (f) Expected regret: top-5 model selection中2 changes表明calibration有practical impact。 Regret reduction 35%源于高contamination model被correctly downranked。\\n\"\n289\t  },\n290\t  {\n291\t    \"name\": \"observational_72b\",\n292\t    \"description\": \"Qwen2.5-72B inference-only observational分析。 No SFT injection(compute prohibitive)——纯推理+signal computation+IRT calibration。 Extends ecological validity to frontier model scale。\\n\",\n293\t    \"results\": {\n294\t      \"raw_mmlu_72B\": 0.847,\n295\t      \"raw_gsm8k_72B\": 0.912,\n296\t      \"raw_arc_72B\": 0.935,\n297\t      \"raw_humaneval_72B\": 0.61,\n298\t      \"S1_exposure_summary_high_pct\": 0.12,\n299\t      \"S2_auc_proxy_72B\": 0.88,\n300\t      \"S4_auc_proxy_72B\": 0.85,\n301\t      \"calibrated_mmlu_72B\": 0.831,\n302\t      \"calibrated_mmlu_ci_lower\": 0.805,\n303\t      \"calibrated_mmlu_ci_upper\": 0.858,\n304\t      \"calibrated_arc_72B\": 0.928,\n305\t      \"calibrated_gsm8k_72B\": 0.908,\n306\t      \"gamma_adjustment_mmlu_pp\": -1.6,\n307\t      \"gamma_adjustment_arc_pp\": -0.7,\n308\t      \"gamma_adjustment_gsm8k_pp\": -0.4,\n309\t      \"inference_time_hours\": 8\n310\t    },\n311\t    \"tables\": [\n312\t      {\n313\t        \"name\": \"Table: 72B Observational Calibration\",\n314\t        \"description\": \"Single model row: Raw vs Calibrated for 4 benchmarks, with 95% CI。 Context row: adjustment magnitude interpretation。\\n\"\n315\t      }\n316\t    ],\n317\t    \"figures\": [],\n318\t    \"analysis\": \"72B observational case extends ContamCal's applicability to frontier models without requiring prohibitive SFT runs。Key finding: even frontier models show detectable contamination signals, with calibrated MMLU -1.6pp suggesting ~2% inflation。 Wide CIs appropriately reflect observational uncertainty。 Framed as ecological validity extension, not primary quantitative validation。\\n\\n\\n(a) 72B raw scores接近ceiling(MMLU 84.7%, ARC 93.5%)。Contamination adjustment 相对modest(MMLU -1.6pp, ARC -0.7pp)——frontier models的high performance partly comes from genuine capability, with moderate contamination inflation。 (b) Signal quality at 72B最强：S2 AUC proxy=0.88, S4=0.85。Largest models have deepest memorization traces and strongest self-evaluation。 (c) CalibrationCI width moderate(MMLU: ±2.7pp)因为observational setting lacks controlled ground truth——IRT model borrows strength from SFT-controlled models但72B θ is extrapolated beyond training data range。 (d) GSM8K adjustment minimal(-0.4pp)——consistent with γ_gsm8k≈0.06 from controlled experiments and 72B's genuine strong reasoning ability。\\n\"\n319\t  },\n320\t  {\n321\t    \"name\": \"closed_weight_2signal_mode\",\n322\t    \"description\": \"Degraded 2-signal mode(ConStat + Self-Critique, no logits/embeddings) for closed-weight models where S1(embedding of training data)和S2(Min-K++, needs logits) 不可用。量化2-signal vs 4-signal calibration accuracy gap。\\n\",\n323\t    \"results\": {\n324\t      \"composite_auc_2sig_3B_mmlu\": 0.79,\n325\t      \"composite_auc_2sig_3B_arc\": 0.82,\n326\t      \"composite_auc_2sig_3B_gsm8k\": 0.74,\n327\t      \"mae_2sig_pp\": 3.4,\n328\t      \"ci_coverage_95_2sig\": 87,\n329\t      \"ci_sharpness_2sig_pp\": 8.2,\n330\t      \"kendall_tau_2sig\": 0.84,\n331\t      \"mae_gap_vs_4sig_pp\": 1.3,\n332\t      \"coverage_gap_vs_4sig_pct\": 5,\n333\t      \"ci_width_ratio_2sig_vs_4sig\": 1.41,\n334\t      \"mae_2sig_vs_dcr_improvement_pp\": 1.2,\n335\t      \"mae_2sig_vs_linear_reg_improvement_pp\": 0.9\n336\t    },\n337\t    \"tables\": [\n338\t      {\n339\t        \"name\": \"Table: 2-signal vs 4-signal Calibration Comparison\",\n340\t        \"description\": \"Two rows(2-sig, 4-sig) × 6 metric columns。 Third row: gap magnitude and significance。\\n\"\n341\t      }\n342\t    ],\n343\t    \"figures\": [],\n344\t    \"analysis\": \"2-signal mode在closed-weight regime仍优于所有non-IRT baselines(MAE 3.4 vs DCR 4.6pp)。 1.3pp gap vs 4-signal mode quantifies the cost of limited model access。 Practical recommendation: use 4-signal when logits available, 2-signal otherwise。 CI width inflation(41%)honestly reflects reduced estimation precision。 Framed as \\\"extensible architecture for future signals\\\" in paper discussion。\\n\\n\\n(a) 2-signal composite AUC 0.79-0.82 at 3B: S3(ConStat)和S4(Self-Critique) 提供complementary information——ConStat检测performance gap between original vs paraphrased items(behavioral signal)，S4检测entropy collapse on familiar items(intrinsic signal)。 两者不依赖logits或training data access，适用于closed-weight APIs。 (b) MAE从2.1pp退化到3.4pp(+1.3pp gap)：lower composite AUC→noisier exposure scores →γ估计less precise→calibration误差增加。但仍优于DCR(4.6pp)1.2pp—— 即使degraded mode, IRT框架的item-level resolution仍有价值。 (c) Coverage降至87%: exposure noise增加但ME model只能部分补偿 (2-signal noise structure不同于4-signal)。CI width增加41%反映更大的estimation uncertainty。 (d) Kendall τ=0.84(vs 4-signal 0.91): ranking preservation仍reasonable但degraded。 高contamination models的calibration less precise导致更多ranking errors。\\n\"\n345\t  },\n346\t  {\n347\t    \"name\": \"multi_family_validation\",\n348\t    \"description\": \"Controlled SFT injection on Llama-3.2-1B at 3 dosage levels(d000/d025/d100)。 验证identifiability boundaries和calibration accuracy跨model family泛化。 Rebuttal-ready experiment。\\n\",\n349\t    \"results\": {\n350\t      \"sft_time_per_run_hours\": 3,\n351\t      \"total_gpu_hours\": 9,\n352\t      \"eval_d000_mmlu\": 0.465,\n353\t      \"eval_d000_arc\": 0.578,\n354\t      \"eval_d000_gsm8k\": 0.342,\n355\t      \"eval_d025_mmlu\": 0.472,\n356\t      \"eval_d025_arc\": 0.589,\n357\t      \"eval_d100_mmlu\": 0.481,\n358\t      \"eval_d100_arc\": 0.602,\n359\t      \"mmlu_inflation_d100_pp\": 1.6,\n360\t      \"arc_inflation_d100_pp\": 2.4,\n361\t      \"S1_auc_llama1B_d005\": 0.96,\n362\t      \"S2_auc_llama1B_d005\": 0.58,\n363\t      \"S4_auc_llama1B_d005\": 0.55,\n364\t      \"cross_family_gamma_k_correlation\": 0.91,\n365\t      \"gamma_k_mmlu_llama\": 0.24,\n366\t      \"gamma_k_arc_llama\": 0.36,\n367\t      \"gamma_k_gsm8k_llama\": 0.05,\n368\t      \"mae_llama_pp\": 2.4,\n369\t      \"ci_coverage_95_llama\": 90,\n370\t      \"fisher_info_threshold_match\": true,\n371\t      \"practical_auc_threshold_llama\": 0.72\n372\t    },\n373\t    \"tables\": [\n374\t      {\n375\t        \"name\": \"Table: Cross-Family γ_k Comparison\",\n376\t        \"description\": \"Rows: MMLU, ARC, GSM8K, HumanEval。 Columns: Qwen γ_k (mean±CI), Llama γ_k (mean±CI), Pearson r。 Bottom: overall correlation r=0.91。\\n\"\n377\t      },\n378\t      {\n379\t        \"name\": \"Table: Identifiability Boundary Cross-Family Comparison\",\n380\t        \"description\": \"Rows: Structural threshold, Practical threshold。 Columns: Qwen(observed), Llama(observed), Fisher Info(predicted)。\\n\"\n381\t      }\n382\t    ],\n383\t    \"figures\": [],\n384\t    \"analysis\": \"Multi-family validation是rebuttal的最强武器。r=0.91 cross-family correlation 表明contamination susceptibility确实是benchmark property——ARC的MC format和limited item pool 使其比MMLU更susceptible(γ_k_ARC > γ_k_MMLU in both families)，GSM8K的open-ended format consistently resistant。Fisher Info thresholds跨family一致性确认theoretical framework的generality。如果reviewer要求\\\"show it works on non-Qwen models\\\"—— 这个实验直接回答，且结论更强(不仅works, 而且quantitatively consistent)。\\n\\n(a) Llama-3.2-1B at ~1B scale介于Qwen2.5-0.5B和1.5B之间。 S2/S4 AUC(0.58/0.55)低于Qwen 1.5B(0.72/0.70)但高于Qwen 0.5B(0.47/0.48)—— 与scale-dependent emergence curve一致，不同architecture在同一capacity range有类似behavior。 (b) Contamination inflation(MMLU +1.6pp, ARC +2.4pp)与Qwen同scale范围一致。 Llama和Qwen在contamination susceptibility上表现similar——confirmation that contamination effect is primarily a capacity/benchmark property, not architecture-specific。 (c) Cross-family γ_k correlation r=0.91: per-benchmark contamination susceptibility ranking高度一致(ARC > MMLU >> GSM8K for both families)。这是\\\"contamination susceptibility is benchmark property\\\"的strongest evidence——如果它是model-family specific, r应该低。 (d) Fisher Info identifiability boundary在Llama上同样成立：practical AUC threshold=0.72 (vs Qwen 0.70)，structural threshold=0.55(identical)——theoretical framework generalizes。 (e) MAE=2.4pp(vs Qwen 2.1pp): slightly worse因为1B scale有noisier signals， 但在best tier range(1.5-3.0pp)内。Coverage 90%也在range。\\n\"\n385\t  }\n386\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9818628c-91c5-4e2f-b68b-f03dd5fc4239","uuid":"158d3160-2e65-47e5-8eaa-373bd56724b7","timestamp":"2026-05-14T19:32:06.240Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_13/projects/contamcal-irt-calibration/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260514T185145/best/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"stage1_signal_pipeline\",\n    \"description\": \"在exp-001产出的全部contaminated+clean模型(0.5B/1.5B/3B × d000/d005/d025/d100 × 2 seeds)上 计算4个detection signals: S1(embedding semantic retrieval), S2(Min-K%++), S3(ConStat performance gap), S4(Self-Critique entropy collapse)。 0.5B数据已完成(exp_002_signals_05B)，此处展开1.5B和3B的预测。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"S1_auc_05B_d005_mmlu\": 0.953,\n      \"S1_auc_05B_d005_gsm8k\": 0.988,\n      \"S1_auc_05B_d005_arc\": 0.995,\n      \"S2_auc_05B_d005_mean\": 0.465,\n      \"S4_auc_05B_d005_mean\": 0.481,\n      \"S1_auc_15B_d005_mmlu\": 0.965,\n      \"S1_auc_15B_d005_gsm8k\": 0.991,\n      \"S1_auc_15B_d005_arc\": 0.996,\n      \"S2_auc_15B_d005_mmlu\": 0.72,\n      \"S2_auc_15B_d005_gsm8k\": 0.68,\n      \"S2_auc_15B_d005_arc\": 0.74,\n      \"S3_auc_15B_d005_mmlu\": 0.67,\n      \"S3_auc_15B_d005_arc\": 0.71,\n      \"S4_auc_15B_d005_mmlu\": 0.7,\n      \"S4_auc_15B_d005_gsm8k\": 0.66,\n      \"S4_auc_15B_d005_arc\": 0.73,\n      \"S1_auc_3B_d005_mmlu\": 0.972,\n      \"S1_auc_3B_d005_gsm8k\": 0.993,\n      \"S1_auc_3B_d005_arc\": 0.997,\n      \"S2_auc_3B_d005_mmlu\": 0.8,\n      \"S2_auc_3B_d005_gsm8k\": 0.76,\n      \"S2_auc_3B_d005_arc\": 0.83,\n      \"S3_auc_3B_d005_mmlu\": 0.74,\n      \"S3_auc_3B_d005_arc\": 0.78,\n      \"S4_auc_3B_d005_mmlu\": 0.77,\n      \"S4_auc_3B_d005_gsm8k\": 0.73,\n      \"S4_auc_3B_d005_arc\": 0.8,\n      \"S2_d100_cohens_d_15B_mmlu\": -1.52,\n      \"S2_d100_cohens_d_15B_arc\": -1.38,\n      \"S2_d100_cohens_d_3B_mmlu\": -2.31,\n      \"S2_d100_cohens_d_3B_arc\": -2.67,\n      \"signal_computation_time_per_model_hours\": 1.5,\n      \"total_gpu_hours\": 18\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Signal AUC × Scale × Dosage Heatmap (d005 within-model)\",\n        \"description\": \"4 signals × 3 scales × 3 benchmarks矩阵。Cells标注AUC值和95% bootstrap CI。 Color coding: green(≥0.70), yellow(0.55-0.70), red(<0.55)。 展示S2/S4从0.5B red到3B green的scale-dependent transition。\\n\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Cross-model Cohen's d at d100 (d100 vs d000)\",\n        \"description\": \"3 signals × 3 scales × 3 benchmarks。标注Cohen's d值和方向箭头。 突出Min-K++ reversal: 0.5B d=-1.98, 3B d=-2.67。\\n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"S2/S4在≥1.5B恢复effectiveness验证了'scale-dependent signal reliability'叙事。 这不仅是empirical observation——它反映了小模型(0.5B)缺乏足够capacity来形成 可检测的memorization痕迹或self-evaluation能力。ARC在所有signals表现最好(items最少、 contamination signal-to-noise ratio最高)。GSM8K的S2/S4 AUC略低于MMLU/ARC， 与open-ended format降低memorization检测力一致。S1保持scale-invariant高AUC(≥0.95) 确认embedding retrieval作为robust anchor signal。Min-K++ reversal随scale增强 (Cohen's d从-1.52到-2.67)是论文最强citation-worthy发现——它证明了naively relying on individual signals can ACTIVELY mislead(不仅仅是fail)。\\n\\n\\nS2(Min-K++)和S4(Self-Critique)的scale-dependent recovery机制： (a) Min-K++依赖token-level perplexity异常检测memorization。0.5B模型容量不足， 即使见过contaminated paraphrases也难以形成持久的token-level记忆痕迹(AUC≈0.47)。 1.5B容量足以保留item-specific记忆，contaminated items呈现显著更低的token surprise(AUC→0.72)。 3B容量充裕，memorization痕迹更清晰(AUC→0.80)。 (b) Self-Critique依赖模型自我评估能力(entropy collapse on seen items)。0.5B的 self-evaluation不可靠(AUC≈0.48)。1.5B emergence of metacognitive capability使得 模型对seen items表现出过度自信(更低entropy)，AUC→0.70。3B self-evaluation更稳定(AUC→0.77)。 (c) S1(embedding retrieval)基于外部sentence-transformer匹配，不依赖目标模型能力， 因此AUC在所有scale一致≥0.95。 (d) Min-K++ d100 reversal持续且scale-dependent：d100将ALL items标记为contaminated， 模型整体token-level distribution向training data shift，导致clean items的perplexity 反而更接近contaminated distribution→Min-K++反向判断。3B模型更充分地拟合d100 training data， reversal更强(Cohen's d=-2.67)。 (e) S3(ConStat)在1.5B/3B恢复，因为larger models对original vs paraphrased items的 performance gap更稳定、更可检测。0.5B的noise floor太高。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"rrf_aggregation_ablation\",\n    \"description\": \"RRF融合4个signals为composite per-item exposure score。 消融实验: (a) RRF vs equal-weight rank averaging, (b) single-signal only (×4), (c) calibration-based weighted RRF, (d) FP injection robustness, (e) degraded 2-signal mode (ConStat+Self-Critique for closed-weight).\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"rrf_composite_auc_05B_d005_mmlu\": 0.955,\n      \"rrf_composite_auc_05B_d005_arc\": 0.995,\n      \"rrf_vs_best_single_delta_05B\": 0.002,\n      \"rrf_composite_auc_15B_d005_mmlu\": 0.975,\n      \"rrf_composite_auc_15B_d005_arc\": 0.998,\n      \"rrf_vs_best_single_delta_15B\": 0.015,\n      \"rrf_composite_auc_3B_d005_mmlu\": 0.985,\n      \"rrf_composite_auc_3B_d005_arc\": 0.999,\n      \"rrf_vs_best_single_delta_3B\": 0.02,\n      \"rrf_vs_equal_weight_delta_auc_3B\": 0.008,\n      \"weighted_rrf_vs_rrf_delta_3B\": 0.003,\n      \"fp_injection_10pct_auc_retention\": 0.96,\n      \"fp_injection_20pct_auc_retention\": 0.91,\n      \"degraded_2signal_auc_3B_mmlu\": 0.79,\n      \"degraded_2signal_auc_3B_arc\": 0.82,\n      \"s1_only_auc_3B_mmlu\": 0.972,\n      \"s2_only_auc_3B_mmlu\": 0.8,\n      \"s3_only_auc_3B_mmlu\": 0.74,\n      \"s4_only_auc_3B_mmlu\": 0.77\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: RRF Ablation Comparison (3B d005)\",\n        \"description\": \"Rows: RRF-4sig, RRF-3sig(no S3), S1-only, S2-only, S3-only, S4-only, equal-weight, weighted-RRF, 2-signal(S3+S4)。 Columns: MMLU AUC, ARC AUC, GSM8K AUC, Mean AUC, Δ vs S1-only。\\n\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: FP Robustness (RRF AUC at varying FP injection rates)\",\n        \"description\": \"Rows: FP rate 0%, 5%, 10%, 15%, 20%。 Columns: MMLU, ARC, GSM8K composite AUC。\\n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"RRF的真正价值在≥1.5B multi-signal regime中显现——当constituent signals各自捕获 不同contamination facets时，rank fusion产生genuine information gain。在0.5B single-signal regime，RRF优雅退化且不引入harm(不比S1-only差)。 Meta-circularity argument得到empirical支持：calibration-based weighting仅+0.3pp， 远不值得引入对training data quality的dependency。Training-free RRF保持设计选择定位。 2-signal mode在3B AUC≥0.79确认closed-weight applicability。\\n\\n\\n(a) 0.5B regime: S2/S3/S4均≈random(AUC<0.55)，RRF退化为S1-only模式。 RRF composite AUC ≈ S1 AUC(+0.002)，因为random signals的RRF ranks 不系统性偏移有效S1的排序。这是graceful degradation——RRF不会因无效信号 而比最佳单信号更差(rank fusion的鲁棒性)。 (b) 1.5B regime: S2/S4恢复(AUC 0.68-0.74)，RRF聚合3-4个above-chance signals。 Rank fusion的互补性在此显现：S1基于training-data proximity，S2基于memorization trace， S4基于metacognition——不同failure modes提供正交information。AUC提升1.5pp over S1-only。 (c) 3B regime: 4个signals全部AUC>0.74，RRF提升2.0pp over S1-only。这是RRF展示 genuine aggregation value的最佳展示区间。 (d) RRF vs equal-weight: RRF对高排名items给予更大权重(reciprocal rank)， 优于uniform averaging 0.8pp——因为top-ranked items的agreement更informative。 (e) Calibration-based weighted RRF仅+0.3pp over vanilla RRF——marginal improvement 不值得引入calibration dependency(meta-circularity argument仍成立)。 (f) FP injection: RRF容忍10% FP rate(AUC保持96%)，20%时下降至91%。 Rank fusion对sparse FP鲁棒因为FP不会系统性地在多个signals中出现。 (g) 2-signal degraded mode(S3+S4, no logits/embeddings): AUC 0.79-0.82 at 3B， sufficient for closed-weight calibration但CI会更宽。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"irt_calibration_and_baselines\",\n    \"description\": \"在exp-001/003产出的controlled models上拟合4PL+γ IRT(Stan NUTS)。 PRIMARY: per-benchmark fitting with per-benchmark γ_k。 ABLATION: joint fitting with global γ, hierarchical γ_k ~ Normal(μ_γ, σ_γ)。 N_models ≥ 30 (3 scales × 4 dosages × 2-3 seeds)。 Compare against 7 baselines。Report 6 evaluation metrics。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"max_rhat\": 1.007,\n      \"min_ess_gamma\": 520,\n      \"min_ess_theta\": 380,\n      \"divergent_transitions\": 0,\n      \"fit_time_mmlu_1000items_min\": 35,\n      \"fit_time_arc_1172items_min\": 28,\n      \"fit_time_gsm8k_1319items_min\": 32,\n      \"n_models_pooled\": 32,\n      \"gamma_k_mmlu_mean\": 0.28,\n      \"gamma_k_mmlu_sd\": 0.06,\n      \"gamma_k_arc_mean\": 0.38,\n      \"gamma_k_arc_sd\": 0.07,\n      \"gamma_k_gsm8k_mean\": 0.06,\n      \"gamma_k_gsm8k_sd\": 0.04,\n      \"gamma_k_humaneval_mean\": 0.12,\n      \"gamma_k_humaneval_sd\": 0.08,\n      \"gamma_k_cv_across_benchmarks\": 0.52,\n      \"gamma_ci_excludes_zero_mmlu\": true,\n      \"gamma_ci_excludes_zero_arc\": true,\n      \"gamma_ci_excludes_zero_gsm8k\": false,\n      \"gamma_ci_excludes_zero_humaneval\": true,\n      \"gamma_ci_excludes_zero_rate\": 0.88,\n      \"mae_contam_cal_pp_mean\": 2.1,\n      \"mae_contam_cal_pp_std\": 0.4,\n      \"ci_coverage_95pct\": 92,\n      \"ci_coverage_80pct\": 82,\n      \"ci_coverage_50pct\": 53,\n      \"ci_sharpness_avg_width_pp\": 5.8,\n      \"kendall_tau\": 0.91,\n      \"dose_response_monotonicity_violations\": 0,\n      \"sbc_rank_uniformity_pvalue\": 0.23,\n      \"mae_mmlu_pp\": 1.8,\n      \"mae_arc_pp\": 2.3,\n      \"mae_gsm8k_pp\": 1.1,\n      \"mae_humaneval_pp\": 3.8,\n      \"mae_raw_no_adjustment_pp\": 9.2,\n      \"mae_remove_rescore_pp\": 6.8,\n      \"mae_single_signal_2pl_gamma_pp\": 3.9,\n      \"mae_vanilla_4pl_no_gamma_pp\": 7.4,\n      \"mae_linear_regression_pp\": 4.3,\n      \"mae_emperor_mitigation_pp\": 8.1,\n      \"mae_dcr_pp\": 4.6,\n      \"mae_improvement_vs_dcr_pp\": 2.5,\n      \"mae_improvement_vs_best_baseline_pp\": 1.8,\n      \"mae_global_gamma_pp\": 3.1,\n      \"mae_hierarchical_gamma_pp\": 2.3,\n      \"hierarchical_mu_gamma\": 0.22,\n      \"hierarchical_sigma_gamma\": 0.14,\n      \"mae_oracle_gamma_pp\": 1.4,\n      \"oracle_vs_estimated_gap_pp\": 0.7,\n      \"ci_coverage_95_me_model\": 93,\n      \"ci_coverage_95_simple_model\": 88,\n      \"ci_sharpness_me_vs_simple_ratio\": 1.12\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Main Results — Calibration Metrics × 8 Methods\",\n        \"description\": \"Rows: Raw, Remove-rescore, Single-signal 2PL+γ, Vanilla 4PL, Linear regression, Emperor mitigation, DCR, ContamCal(ours)。 Columns: MAE(pp)±bootstrap CI, 95% Coverage, 80% Coverage, CI Width(pp), Kendall τ, Monotonicity violations。Bolded: ContamCal wins on all metrics。 Bottom row: Δ vs DCR with significance marker。\\n\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Per-benchmark γ_k Estimates\",\n        \"description\": \"Rows: MMLU, ARC-Challenge, GSM8K, HumanEval。 Columns: γ_k posterior mean, 95% CI, CI excludes 0?, effect size interpretation。 Highlight: CV(γ_k)=0.52，支撑'contamination susceptibility is benchmark property'。\\n\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Calibration Metrics Decomposed by Benchmark\",\n        \"description\": \"Rows: 4 benchmarks。Columns: MAE, Coverage, Sharpness, per-benchmark notes。 GSM8K row highlighted as negative control (γ≈0, MAE lowest)。\\n\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Model Ablation — Global γ vs Per-benchmark γ_k vs Hierarchical\",\n        \"description\": \"3 rows × same metric columns。Per-benchmark γ_k primary; global γ loses 1.0pp MAE; hierarchical γ_k intermediate (formal heterogeneity test)。\\n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"exp-006是论文核心实验。MAE=2.1pp(±0.4)显著优于DCR的4.6pp(Δ=2.5pp, p<0.01 bootstrap test)。 Coverage 92%接近但未达95% nominal——SBC p=0.23确认这不是model misspecification， 而是local independence violation的已知IRT limitation(single model→correlated item responses)。 ME model部分弥补(88%→93%)但complete correction需要更复杂的correlated-error model (超出本文scope，acknowledged in Limitations)。Per-benchmark γ_k的CV=0.52是 论文的structural insight——contamination susceptibility取决于benchmark format和content characteristics， 不是model property。Oracle γ分析(gap=0.7pp)量化了detection signal quality的calibration ceiling—— future work的better signals可directly translate to tighter calibration。\\n\\n\\n(a) NUTS收敛(R̂<1.01, ESS>400): exp-004 simulation sweep已在N=50/AUC=0.80验证 MCMC quality(0 divergence, max R̂=1.010, min ESS=439)。Real data N=32(multi-seed pooling) 在simulation验证范围内。MMLU subsampled至1000 items降低计算负担同时保留statistical power。 (b) Per-benchmark γ_k heterogeneity(CV=0.52): ARC γ_k=0.38最大——science reasoning MC items 格式固定且答案模式可记忆，contamination直接提升正确选项probability。MMLU γ_k=0.28中等—— 14K items diversity dilutes per-item memorization benefit。GSM8K γ_k≈0.06—— open-ended generation format天然抵抗contamination(即使见过问题，仍需自主推理得出答案)， 正确扮演negative control角色。HumanEval γ_k=0.12小——code generation部分受益于pattern recall 但functional correctness仍需正确逻辑。 (c) γ CI排除0的rate=0.88(≈7/8 benchmark-conditions排除0)：MMLU/ARC/HumanEval排除0， GSM8K不排除(γ≈0.06±0.04, CI包含0)。这恰好验证了negative control和contamination susceptibility is benchmark property的论点。 (d) MAE=2.1pp: IRT通过item-level response patterns检测contamination效应——即使 average benchmark accuracy change仅1-2pp(1.5B/3B MMLU)，contaminated items呈现 concentrated 15-20pp per-item accuracy boost(被95% uncontaminated items稀释)。 IRT的γ_k × e_ij项精确捕获这种item-level effect。Counterfactual(e=0)移除此effect 后recovery误差主要来自：(i)θ-γ posterior correlation残余(~0.5pp)， (ii)item subsample noise for MMLU(~0.3pp)，(iii)per-item exposure score noise(~0.5pp)。 (e) CI coverage 92% vs nominal 95%: 3pp gap的主要来源是local independence violation (single model responds to all items→item responses correlated through shared parameters)。 ME model通过propagating exposure noise部分补偿(88%→93%)。SBC诊断p=0.23确认 model specification本身正确(coverage gap来自local independence, not model misspecification)。 (f) Kendall τ=0.91: 校准后model ranking高度保留。少量ranking变化来自high-dosage models的calibration adjustment。 (g) Dose-response monotonicity: γ effect单调递增(d005<d025<d100)，0 violations。 0.5B的negative overall accuracy与positive γ共存不违反单调性——γ衡量的是per-item contamination benefit(正)，而θ降低反映overall SFT degradation(负)。 (h) DCR MAE=4.6pp vs ContamCal 2.1pp: DCR缺乏per-item resolution和Bayesian UQ， 只能做benchmark-level fuzzy adjustment。Linear regression MAE=4.3pp因为linear assumption 不能捕获IRT的nonlinear item-response relationship。 (i) Oracle γ gap=0.7pp: exposure score noise贡献了~0.7pp MAE overhead， 说明signal quality是calibration precision的binding constraint。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"scale_bridging_7b\",\n    \"description\": \"Qwen2.5-7B controlled SFT injection at 4 dosage levels(d000/d005/d025/d100)。 验证calibration accuracy和signal effectiveness scaling至7B。 LoRA SFT on 1×H100, ~6h per run。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"sft_time_per_run_hours\": 6.5,\n      \"total_gpu_hours\": 26,\n      \"sft_d000_final_loss\": 0.92,\n      \"sft_d100_final_loss\": 0.98,\n      \"eval_d000_mmlu\": 0.735,\n      \"eval_d000_gsm8k\": 0.798,\n      \"eval_d000_arc\": 0.874,\n      \"eval_d000_humaneval\": 0.268,\n      \"eval_d005_mmlu\": 0.742,\n      \"eval_d005_gsm8k\": 0.801,\n      \"eval_d005_arc\": 0.882,\n      \"eval_d025_mmlu\": 0.756,\n      \"eval_d025_arc\": 0.893,\n      \"eval_d100_mmlu\": 0.779,\n      \"eval_d100_gsm8k\": 0.806,\n      \"eval_d100_arc\": 0.908,\n      \"eval_d100_humaneval\": 0.28,\n      \"mmlu_inflation_pp\": 4.4,\n      \"arc_inflation_pp\": 3.4,\n      \"gsm8k_inflation_pp\": 0.8,\n      \"S1_auc_7B_d005_mean\": 0.978,\n      \"S2_auc_7B_d005_mean\": 0.85,\n      \"S4_auc_7B_d005_mean\": 0.82,\n      \"S2_d100_cohens_d_7B\": -2.85,\n      \"mae_with_7B_pp\": 2.0,\n      \"ci_coverage_95_with_7B\": 93,\n      \"gamma_k_mmlu_with_7B\": 0.31,\n      \"gamma_k_arc_with_7B\": 0.4\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: 7B Dose-Response Accuracy\",\n        \"description\": \"Rows: d000, d005, d025, d100。Columns: MMLU, ARC, GSM8K, HumanEval。 Compare inflation pattern with 0.5B/1.5B/3B。\\n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"7B数据是scale-bridging的关键——它证明了contamination inflation随model capacity增长， 在practical model sizes(7B)处达到可测量且需要校准的水平(MMLU +4.4pp)。 同时S2/S4 AUC进一步提升验证了scale-dependent signal narrative的completeness。 7B加入IRT pool后calibration quality marginal improvement表明N=32已接近saturation。\\n\\n\\n(a) 7B contamination inflation更大(MMLU +4.4pp, ARC +3.4pp vs 1.5B/3B的<2pp)： 7B capacity足以在LoRA SFT中同时维持general capability和memorize contaminated items。 0.5B/1.5B/3B的smaller capacity forced a tradeoff(0.5B: memorization hurts general, 1.5B/3B: memorization barely helps)。7B跨过了capacity threshold使memorization productively translate to benchmark inflation。这验证了contamination是real-world concern at practical model scales。 (b) GSM8K inflation仅0.8pp：7B对GSM8K的CoT reasoning在SFT后保持稳定(vs 3B catastrophic forgetting)，但open-ended format仍然抵抗contamination inflation。 (c) S2/S4 AUC在7B进一步提升(S2: 0.85, S4: 0.82)：更大模型的memorization痕迹更深， token-level signals更清晰。Min-K++ reversal也更强(Cohen's d=-2.85)——7B更充分拟合 d100 training data distribution。 (d) Adding 7B to IRT pool(N_models→38-40)改善calibration(MAE 2.1→2.0pp, coverage 92→93%)： 更多examinees + wider ability range改善θ estimation和γ identifiability。 γ_k_mmlu增加(0.28→0.31)因为7B贡献了更清晰的contamination signal。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"signal_survival_analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"系统评估detection signal reliability across scales和dosages。 0.5B数据已完成(exp_008_signal_survival_v4)。 扩展到1.5B/3B + Instruct/RL proxy models。 输出: signal × scale × dosage AUC heatmap(论文Figure 2)。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"S1_d005_auc_05B_mean\": 0.979,\n      \"S2_d005_auc_05B_mean\": 0.465,\n      \"S4_d005_auc_05B_mean\": 0.481,\n      \"S1_d100_cross_cohens_d_05B\": 3.6,\n      \"S2_d100_cross_cohens_d_05B\": -1.98,\n      \"S4_d100_cross_cohens_d_05B\": 0.45,\n      \"effective_signals_at_05B\": 1,\n      \"S1_d005_auc_15B_mean\": 0.97,\n      \"S2_d005_auc_15B_mean\": 0.72,\n      \"S4_d005_auc_15B_mean\": 0.7,\n      \"S1_d100_cross_cohens_d_15B\": 3.85,\n      \"S2_d100_cross_cohens_d_15B\": -1.52,\n      \"S4_d100_cross_cohens_d_15B\": 0.88,\n      \"effective_signals_at_15B\": 3,\n      \"S1_d005_auc_3B_mean\": 0.98,\n      \"S2_d005_auc_3B_mean\": 0.8,\n      \"S4_d005_auc_3B_mean\": 0.77,\n      \"S1_d100_cross_cohens_d_3B\": 4.2,\n      \"S2_d100_cross_cohens_d_3B\": -2.31,\n      \"S4_d100_cross_cohens_d_3B\": 1.15,\n      \"effective_signals_at_3B\": 3,\n      \"S4_instruct_vs_base_sensitivity\": 0.68,\n      \"S2_instruct_degradation_pct\": 15,\n      \"S1_instruct_stable\": true,\n      \"s2_auc_070_threshold_scale\": \"~1.2B (interpolated)\",\n      \"s4_auc_070_threshold_scale\": \"~1.4B (interpolated)\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Full Signal × Scale × Dosage AUC Matrix\",\n        \"description\": \"Grand matrix: 3 signals(S1/S2/S4) × 3 scales(0.5B/1.5B/3B) × 3 dosages(d005/d025/d100) × 3 benchmarks(MMLU/ARC/GSM8K)。d005 cells = within-model AUC; d100 cells = cross-model Cohen's d。Color: green/yellow/red threshold coding。\\n\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Instruct/RL Proxy Signal Comparison\",\n        \"description\": \"Rows: Base, Instruct, RL-proxy。Columns: S1/S2/S4 sensitivity metrics。\\n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"exp-008是Core Contribution #2的实证基础。3个key findings： (1) Scale-dependent emergence: S2/S4从0.5B random(AUC≈0.47)到3B effective(AUC≈0.80/0.77)， transition at ~1.2-1.4B。这不是arbitrary——对应LLM capability emergence in memorization and metacognition。 (2) Min-K++ reversal(d=-1.98 at 0.5B, d=-2.31 at 3B): 最强citation-worthy发现。 Warning: naive use of Min-K++ at high contamination ACTIVELY MISLEADS。机制analysis (全量memorization→perplexity distribution shift→reversal)提供explanatory depth。 (3) Item-level vs cross-model detection范式区分：d005用within-model AUC(item discrimination)， d100用cross-model Cohen's d(model discrimination)。d100 AUC=0.5是labeling artifact (all items contaminated→no discriminative labels)，不是signal failure。\\n\\n\\n(a) Signal survival pattern由model capacity驱动：0.5B缺乏token-level memorization depth(S2 fails)和metacognitive self-evaluation(S4 fails)。1.5B是transition point—— S2/S4 emergent capabilities使AUC跨过0.70 practical threshold。3B consolidates。 S1(embedding retrieval)依赖external encoder，始终stable。 (b) Min-K++ reversal机制：d100将所有items加入training data，模型的token-level distribution 整体shift。Min-K++基于\\\"low perplexity tokens\\\"检测memorization，但当EVERYTHING is memorized， baseline perplexity distribution itself shifts→clean items的relative perplexity paradoxically更接近contaminated profile→reversal。3B模型更充分学习d100 distribution→ reversal更强(d=-2.31 vs 0.5B d=-1.98)。 (c) S4(Self-Critique)d100 cross-model Cohen's d从0.5B=0.45增至3B=1.15： larger models的self-evaluation对contaminated items更consistently confident， cross-model effect size增长。 (d) Instruct/RL proxy: Instruct models经过RLHF/DPO，token-level distributions 进一步shift。S2(Min-K++)在Instruct models上AUC降低~15%(perplexity patterns被RLHF扰动)， 但S4(Self-Critique)在Instruct models上因为enhanced instruction-following能力 实际上更有效(sensitivity=0.68)。S1保持stable因为embedding retrieval不依赖target model。 (e) Scale transition thresholds通过linear interpolation估计：S2在~1.2B达到AUC=0.70， S4在~1.4B。这与LLM capability emergence literature一致。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"rl_observational_case_study\",\n    \"description\": \"对existing RL-trained models (Qwen2.5-Instruct 0.5B/1.5B/3B/7B, DeepSeek-R1-Distill-1.5B/7B) 应用ContamCal pipeline。 Observational study——directional external validity, not full quantitative validation。 Near-zero γ check on known-clean benchmark作为specificity test。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"S1_auc_instruct_3B\": 0.94,\n      \"S2_auc_instruct_3B\": 0.62,\n      \"S4_auc_instruct_3B\": 0.71,\n      \"S1_auc_deepseek_r1_7B\": 0.91,\n      \"gamma_mmlu_instruct_models\": 0.18,\n      \"gamma_mmlu_instruct_ci_width\": 0.22,\n      \"gamma_arc_instruct_models\": 0.25,\n      \"gamma_arc_instruct_ci_width\": 0.19,\n      \"gamma_mmlu_deepseek_r1\": 0.14,\n      \"gamma_mmlu_deepseek_ci_width\": 0.28,\n      \"gamma_clean_benchmark_mean\": 0.02,\n      \"gamma_clean_benchmark_ci_includes_zero\": true,\n      \"specificity_pass\": true,\n      \"top5_selection_changes_uncal_vs_cal\": 2,\n      \"top5_selection_changes_cal_vs_remove_rescore\": 1,\n      \"regret_reduction_pct\": 35,\n      \"ci_width_rl_vs_sft_ratio\": 1.8\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: RL Model Calibration Results\",\n        \"description\": \"Rows: 6 RL models。Columns: Raw score, Calibrated score, 95% CI, γ estimate, Signal AUC(S1/S2/S4), CI width ratio vs SFT。\\n\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Expected Regret Analysis\",\n        \"description\": \"Top-5 rankings under: Raw, Remove-rescore, ContamCal。 Highlight position changes and regret scores。\\n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Observational case study提供directional external validity。Key insights: (1) RL post-training partially但未完全消除SFT-phase contamination(γ>0 for RL models)。 (2) ContamCal honestly widens CIs when signal quality degrades(CI width ratio 1.8×)—— 这是feature not bug，正确反映epistemic uncertainty。 (3) Specificity test通过确认framework不会over-calibrate clean benchmarks。 (4) 2 top-5 ranking changes demonstrate practical impact for model selection decisions。 Framed as \\\"directional\\\"——no ground truth for RL models, acknowledged in Limitations。\\n\\n\\n(a) Signal quality on RL models degraded但non-trivially：RLHF/DPO改变token-level distributions使S2(Min-K++)AUC降至0.62(from SFT baseline ~0.80 at 3B)——RL optimization partially erases memorization traces。S4(Self-Critique)更robust(AUC=0.71)因为 RLHF actually enhances self-evaluation capability。S1(embedding)保持高AUC(0.94) 因为independent of target model。 (b) γ estimates with wide CIs(width 0.19-0.28 vs SFT的~0.06-0.08)： RL models的exposure scores更noisy(S2 degraded)→ME model propagates这些noise into wider posteriors。这是honest uncertainty——calibration精度受限于input signal quality， 系统正确报告了这种limitation。 (c) Instruct models γ_mmlu=0.18(moderate)：RL post-training未fully消除SFT-phase contamination。Qwen2.5-Instruct很可能在SFT phase包含了benchmark-adjacent data。 γ比controlled SFT experiments低(0.28)因为RL optimization partially corrects memorized shortcuts。 (d) DeepSeek-R1-Distill γ=0.14 with wider CI：reasoning-distilled model的contamination profile不同于standard RLHF。更宽CI反映更不确定的exposure estimation。 (e) Specificity pass(γ_clean≈0.02, CI includes 0)：关键validation——ContamCal不会 对genuinely clean benchmarks产生false positive校准adjustment。 (f) Expected regret: top-5 model selection中2 changes表明calibration有practical impact。 Regret reduction 35%源于高contamination model被correctly downranked。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"observational_72b\",\n    \"description\": \"Qwen2.5-72B inference-only observational分析。 No SFT injection(compute prohibitive)——纯推理+signal computation+IRT calibration。 Extends ecological validity to frontier model scale。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"raw_mmlu_72B\": 0.847,\n      \"raw_gsm8k_72B\": 0.912,\n      \"raw_arc_72B\": 0.935,\n      \"raw_humaneval_72B\": 0.61,\n      \"S1_exposure_summary_high_pct\": 0.12,\n      \"S2_auc_proxy_72B\": 0.88,\n      \"S4_auc_proxy_72B\": 0.85,\n      \"calibrated_mmlu_72B\": 0.831,\n      \"calibrated_mmlu_ci_lower\": 0.805,\n      \"calibrated_mmlu_ci_upper\": 0.858,\n      \"calibrated_arc_72B\": 0.928,\n      \"calibrated_gsm8k_72B\": 0.908,\n      \"gamma_adjustment_mmlu_pp\": -1.6,\n      \"gamma_adjustment_arc_pp\": -0.7,\n      \"gamma_adjustment_gsm8k_pp\": -0.4,\n      \"inference_time_hours\": 8\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: 72B Observational Calibration\",\n        \"description\": \"Single model row: Raw vs Calibrated for 4 benchmarks, with 95% CI。 Context row: adjustment magnitude interpretation。\\n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"72B observational case extends ContamCal's applicability to frontier models without requiring prohibitive SFT runs。Key finding: even frontier models show detectable contamination signals, with calibrated MMLU -1.6pp suggesting ~2% inflation。 Wide CIs appropriately reflect observational uncertainty。 Framed as ecological validity extension, not primary quantitative validation。\\n\\n\\n(a) 72B raw scores接近ceiling(MMLU 84.7%, ARC 93.5%)。Contamination adjustment 相对modest(MMLU -1.6pp, ARC -0.7pp)——frontier models的high performance partly comes from genuine capability, with moderate contamination inflation。 (b) Signal quality at 72B最强：S2 AUC proxy=0.88, S4=0.85。Largest models have deepest memorization traces and strongest self-evaluation。 (c) CalibrationCI width moderate(MMLU: ±2.7pp)因为observational setting lacks controlled ground truth——IRT model borrows strength from SFT-controlled models但72B θ is extrapolated beyond training data range。 (d) GSM8K adjustment minimal(-0.4pp)——consistent with γ_gsm8k≈0.06 from controlled experiments and 72B's genuine strong reasoning ability。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"closed_weight_2signal_mode\",\n    \"description\": \"Degraded 2-signal mode(ConStat + Self-Critique, no logits/embeddings) for closed-weight models where S1(embedding of training data)和S2(Min-K++, needs logits) 不可用。量化2-signal vs 4-signal calibration accuracy gap。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"composite_auc_2sig_3B_mmlu\": 0.79,\n      \"composite_auc_2sig_3B_arc\": 0.82,\n      \"composite_auc_2sig_3B_gsm8k\": 0.74,\n      \"mae_2sig_pp\": 3.4,\n      \"ci_coverage_95_2sig\": 87,\n      \"ci_sharpness_2sig_pp\": 8.2,\n      \"kendall_tau_2sig\": 0.84,\n      \"mae_gap_vs_4sig_pp\": 1.3,\n      \"coverage_gap_vs_4sig_pct\": 5,\n      \"ci_width_ratio_2sig_vs_4sig\": 1.41,\n      \"mae_2sig_vs_dcr_improvement_pp\": 1.2,\n      \"mae_2sig_vs_linear_reg_improvement_pp\": 0.9\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: 2-signal vs 4-signal Calibration Comparison\",\n        \"description\": \"Two rows(2-sig, 4-sig) × 6 metric columns。 Third row: gap magnitude and significance。\\n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"2-signal mode在closed-weight regime仍优于所有non-IRT baselines(MAE 3.4 vs DCR 4.6pp)。 1.3pp gap vs 4-signal mode quantifies the cost of limited model access。 Practical recommendation: use 4-signal when logits available, 2-signal otherwise。 CI width inflation(41%)honestly reflects reduced estimation precision。 Framed as \\\"extensible architecture for future signals\\\" in paper discussion。\\n\\n\\n(a) 2-signal composite AUC 0.79-0.82 at 3B: S3(ConStat)和S4(Self-Critique) 提供complementary information——ConStat检测performance gap between original vs paraphrased items(behavioral signal)，S4检测entropy collapse on familiar items(intrinsic signal)。 两者不依赖logits或training data access，适用于closed-weight APIs。 (b) MAE从2.1pp退化到3.4pp(+1.3pp gap)：lower composite AUC→noisier exposure scores →γ估计less precise→calibration误差增加。但仍优于DCR(4.6pp)1.2pp—— 即使degraded mode, IRT框架的item-level resolution仍有价值。 (c) Coverage降至87%: exposure noise增加但ME model只能部分补偿 (2-signal noise structure不同于4-signal)。CI width增加41%反映更大的estimation uncertainty。 (d) Kendall τ=0.84(vs 4-signal 0.91): ranking preservation仍reasonable但degraded。 高contamination models的calibration less precise导致更多ranking errors。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"multi_family_validation\",\n    \"description\": \"Controlled SFT injection on Llama-3.2-1B at 3 dosage levels(d000/d025/d100)。 验证identifiability boundaries和calibration accuracy跨model family泛化。 Rebuttal-ready experiment。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"sft_time_per_run_hours\": 3,\n      \"total_gpu_hours\": 9,\n      \"eval_d000_mmlu\": 0.465,\n      \"eval_d000_arc\": 0.578,\n      \"eval_d000_gsm8k\": 0.342,\n      \"eval_d025_mmlu\": 0.472,\n      \"eval_d025_arc\": 0.589,\n      \"eval_d100_mmlu\": 0.481,\n      \"eval_d100_arc\": 0.602,\n      \"mmlu_inflation_d100_pp\": 1.6,\n      \"arc_inflation_d100_pp\": 2.4,\n      \"S1_auc_llama1B_d005\": 0.96,\n      \"S2_auc_llama1B_d005\": 0.58,\n      \"S4_auc_llama1B_d005\": 0.55,\n      \"cross_family_gamma_k_correlation\": 0.91,\n      \"gamma_k_mmlu_llama\": 0.24,\n      \"gamma_k_arc_llama\": 0.36,\n      \"gamma_k_gsm8k_llama\": 0.05,\n      \"mae_llama_pp\": 2.4,\n      \"ci_coverage_95_llama\": 90,\n      \"fisher_info_threshold_match\": true,\n      \"practical_auc_threshold_llama\": 0.72\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Cross-Family γ_k Comparison\",\n        \"description\": \"Rows: MMLU, ARC, GSM8K, HumanEval。 Columns: Qwen γ_k (mean±CI), Llama γ_k (mean±CI), Pearson r。 Bottom: overall correlation r=0.91。\\n\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Identifiability Boundary Cross-Family Comparison\",\n        \"description\": \"Rows: Structural threshold, Practical threshold。 Columns: Qwen(observed), Llama(observed), Fisher Info(predicted)。\\n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Multi-family validation是rebuttal的最强武器。r=0.91 cross-family correlation 表明contamination susceptibility确实是benchmark property——ARC的MC format和limited item pool 使其比MMLU更susceptible(γ_k_ARC > γ_k_MMLU in both families)，GSM8K的open-ended format consistently resistant。Fisher Info thresholds跨family一致性确认theoretical framework的generality。如果reviewer要求\\\"show it works on non-Qwen models\\\"—— 这个实验直接回答，且结论更强(不仅works, 而且quantitatively consistent)。\\n\\n(a) Llama-3.2-1B at ~1B scale介于Qwen2.5-0.5B和1.5B之间。 S2/S4 AUC(0.58/0.55)低于Qwen 1.5B(0.72/0.70)但高于Qwen 0.5B(0.47/0.48)—— 与scale-dependent emergence curve一致，不同architecture在同一capacity range有类似behavior。 (b) Contamination inflation(MMLU +1.6pp, ARC +2.4pp)与Qwen同scale范围一致。 Llama和Qwen在contamination susceptibility上表现similar——confirmation that contamination effect is primarily a capacity/benchmark property, not architecture-specific。 (c) Cross-family γ_k correlation r=0.91: per-benchmark contamination susceptibility ranking高度一致(ARC > MMLU >> GSM8K for both families)。这是\\\"contamination susceptibility is benchmark property\\\"的strongest evidence——如果它是model-family specific, r应该低。 (d) Fisher Info identifiability boundary在Llama上同样成立：practical AUC threshold=0.72 (vs Qwen 0.70)，structural threshold=0.55(identical)——theoretical framework generalizes。 (e) MAE=2.4pp(vs Qwen 2.1pp): slightly worse因为1B scale有noisier signals， 但在best tier range(1.5-3.0pp)内。Coverage 90%也在range。\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":386,"startLine":1,"totalLines":386}}}
